e she knew her confession would make no difference now."}],"answer":"B"},{"n":10,"stem":"Overall, the article suggests that","options":[{"key":"A","text":"cheating is not limited to schools or exams."},{"key":"B","text":"it is more widespread in schools than elsewhere."},{"key":"C","text":"people should try and do something about this problem."},{"key":"D","text":"people should learn to live with this problem."}],"answer":"A"}]}$mtr$::jsonb) on conflict (task_id) do update set task = excluded.task;
insert into public.tasks (id, exam_id, section, number, kind, exam_type, points, position, content, audio) values ($mtr$2006-febr-kozep-R3$mtr$, $mtr$2006-febr-kozep$mtr$, $mtr$reading$mtr$, 3, $mtr$bank$mtr$, $mtr$mondat visszahelyezése szövegbe$mtr$, 10, 3, $mtr${"id":"2006-febr-kozep-R3","number":3,"kind":"bank","layout":"inline","examType":"mondat visszahelyezése szövegbe","points":10,"instructions":["Read this story of an archaeological scandal.","Some words have been left out from the text.","Your task is to fill in the gaps from the list below the text.","Remember that there are two extra letters that you do not need."],"title":"The Dinosaur that Fooled the World","body":["In February 1999, at a fair in Arizona, an amazing fossil from China came on to the market. It was priced at $80,000 and only the {{0}} were invited to see it. It had the {{11}} of a bird and the tail of a dinosaur. It had all the {{12}} of one of the most sought-after fossils in all palaeontology – the missing link that proved {{13}} that dinosaurs evolved into birds. One of the world’s {{14}} magazines became involved. In exchange for an exclusive story, it agreed to fund the analysis of the fossil. A team of top experts {{15}} were assembled to examine the new discovery – and declared it was a {{16}}, archaeoraptor lianoningensis.","However, after a detective story that followed the path across China, the {{17}} emerged. The fossil was a fake. It had been constructed out of {{18}} of several different animals. One of the world’s most respected popular science journals had made a terrible mistake.","The story has one final twist, though. The faker had missed the {{19}} of his material. Two of the fragments that had been used to make the fake may in fact be from {{20}} that are part bird, part dinosaur – the phoney fossil may in fact contain two missing links."],"bank":[{"key":"A","text":"awful truth"},{"key":"B","text":"characteristics"},{"key":"C","text":"creatures"},{"key":"D","text":"fragments"},{"key":"E","text":"head and body"},{"key":"F","text":"in the field"},{"key":"G","text":"very top dealers"},{"key":"H","text":"new species"},{"key":"I","text":"big row"},{"key":"K","text":"great surprise"},{"key":"L","text":"real value"},{"key":"M","text":"most prestigious"},{"key":"N","text":"once and for all"}],"items":[{"n":0,"example":true,"answer":"G"},{"n":11},{"n":12},{"n":13},{"n":14},{"n":15},{"n":16},{"n":17},{"n":18},{"n":19},{"n":20}]}$mtr$::jsonb, null)
insert into public.task_keys (task_id, task) values ($mtr$2006-febr-kozep-R3$mtr$, $mtr${"id":"2006-febr-kozep-R3","number":3,"kind":"bank","layout":"inline","examType":"mondat visszahelyezése szövegbe","points":10,"instructions":["Read this story of an archaeological scandal.","Some words have been left out from the text.","Your task is to fill in the gaps from the list below the text.","Remember that there are two extra letters that you do not need."],"title":"The Dinosaur that Fooled the World","body":["In February 1999, at a fair in Arizona, an amazing fossil from China came on to the market. It was priced at $80,000 and only the {{0}} were invited to see it. It had the {{11}} of a bird and the tail of a dinosaur. It had all the {{12}} of one of the most sought-after fossils in all palaeontology – the missing link that proved {{13}} that dinosaurs evolved into birds. One of the world’s {{14}} magazines became involved. In exchange for an exclusive story, it agreed to fund the analysis of the fossil. A team of top experts {{15}} were assembled to examine the new discovery – and declared it was a {{16}}, archaeoraptor lianoningensis.","However, after a detective story that followed the path across China, the {{17}} emerged. The fossil was a fake. It had been constructed out of {{18}} of several different animals. One of the world’s most respected popular science journals had made a terrible mistake.","The story has one final twist, though. The faker had missed the {{19}} of his material. Two of the fragments that had been used to make the fake may in fact be from {{20}} that are part bird, part dinosaur – the phoney fossil may in fact contain two missing links."],"bank":[{"key":"A","text":"awful truth"},{"key":"B","text":"characteristics"},{"key":"C","text":"creatures"},{"key":"D","text":"fragments"},{"key":"E","text":"head and body"},{"key":"F","text":"in the field"},{"key":"G","text":"very top dealers"},{"key":"H","text":"new species"},{"key":"I","text":"big row"},{"key":"K","text":"great surprise"},{"key":"L","text":"real value"},{"key":"M","text":"most prestigious"},{"key":"N","text":"once and for all"}],"items":[{"n":0,"example":true,"answer":"G"},{"n":11,"answer":"E"},{"n":12,"answer":"B"},{"n":13,"answer":"N"},{"n":14,"answer":"M"},{"n":15,"answer":"F"},{"n":16,"answer":"H"},{"n":17,"answer":"A"},{"n":18,"answer":"D"},{"n":19,"answer":"L"},{"n":20,"answer":"C"}]}$mtr$::jsonb) on conflict (task_id) do update set task = excluded.task;
insert into public.tasks (id, exam_id, section, number, kind, exam_type, points, position, content, audio) values ($mtr$2006-febr-kozep-R4$mtr$, $mtr$2006-febr-kozep$mtr$, $mtr$reading$mtr$, 4, $mtr$text$mtr$, $mtr$mondat vagy összefoglaló kiegészítése a szöveg alapján$mtr$, 10, 4, $mtr${"id":"2006-febr-kozep-R4","number":4,"kind":"text","layout":"inline","examType":"mondat vagy összefoglaló kiegészítése a szöveg alapján","points":10,"instructions":["Read this article on some funny mistakes in films and then read the gapped sentences.","Your task is to fill the gaps with one or two words only according to the information in the article."],"title":"Cut! It’s another blunder on set","body":["It has been branded the funniest foul-up in Hollywood blockbuster history. In the first Star Wars film, evil stormtroopers break into a control room where the heroes are holed up. But if you watch closely, one soldier coming through the doorway bangs his head so hard he almost knocks himself out.","The incident has topped a new poll of movie blunders. The mistakes on the list, compiled by DVD rental firm Silverscreen, are a mixture of glaring continuity errors and on- camera blunders.","The advent of DVD players, which allow viewers to pause films frame by frame, has boosted the spotting of celluloid howlers.","In second place behind Star Wars is Commando, starring Arnold Schwarzenegger as an ex-special forces soldier apparently immune to bullets. He completely destroys one side of his yellow Porsche – yet moments later he is seen driving away in a pristine vehicle.","At No 3 is a gaffe in Ridley Scott’s Gladiator which reveals a production member in blue jeans standing behind Russell Crowe who is dressed in Roman regalia.","In fourth place is Charlie’s Angels. During one of the fight scenes, star Drew Barrymore tries to get Lucy Liu’s attention by calling out “Lucy” even though her character’s name is Alex.","Fifth is the Matrix. While Neo, played by Keanu Reeves, is being interrogated by Agent Smith his mouth is sealed. However, when the camera focuses on Smith his glasses show a reflection of Neo sitting down completely unharmed.","In sixth place comes Spider Man. Two muggers are thrown through two windows, but shortly afterwards the windows are intact.","Seventh is Terminator 3 – Rise of the Machines. While John and Catherine are in the aircraft hangar the tail number on the Cessna is N3035C. In the air the number shown is N9373F and when it lands it goes back to N3035C.","A No 8 is Harry Potter and the Philosopher’s Stone. After end-of-year exams Harry, Ron and Hermione rush to Hagrid. One of Harry’s lines finishes with, “Why didn’t I see it before?” But Hermione is behind him mouthing the lines.","Ninth is Black Hawk Down. When a Humvee pulls up to let someone cross the street viewers can see one of the crew members driving the car wearing a white T-shirt. But all the people who got into the car were wearing fatigues.","And last at No10 is The Rocky Horror Picture Show. While a criminologist talks about an event he describes it as “a late November evening”. However, later on, Brad and Janet are driving with the radio on and US President Nixon’s resignation is being broadcast. Nixon resigned in August 1974.","In the first line of the article the word {{0}} is a synonym for blunder or mistake.","In a George Lucas film a soldier hurts {{21}} instead of the enemy.","In the first four paragraphs of the article one more synonym for blunders, foul-ups, mistakes or errors is {{22}}.","After the crash in Commando, the hero’s {{23}} shouldn’t be seen in perfect condition.","In this historical film, viewers shouldn’t be able to see the {{24}} of one of the staff.","In Charlie’s Angels the actress’s {{25}} shouldn’t be heard.","A mistake in the interrogation scene in The Matrix means the viewers can see that the hero is {{26}}.","The windows should have been {{27}} after this incident in Spider Man.","In Terminator 3 it looks as if John and Catherine had got into a different {{28}} while they were in midair.","In a scene in The Philosopher’s Stone you can hear Harry Potter speaking, and at the same time you can also read the words on {{29}} lips.","In Black Hawk Down it is a staff member’s {{30}} that gives him away."],"grading":{"spelling":"lenient"},"items":[{"n":0,"example":true,"accept":["foul-up"]},{"n":21},{"n":22},{"n":23},{"n":24},{"n":25},{"n":26},{"n":27},{"n":28},{"n":29},{"n":30}]}$mtr$::jsonb, null)
insert into public.task_keys (task_id, task) values ($mtr$2006-febr-kozep-R4$mtr$, $mtr${"id":"2006-febr-kozep-R4","number":4,"kind":"text","layout":"inline","examType":"mondat vagy összefoglaló kiegészítése a szöveg alapján","points":10,"instructions":["Read this article on some funny mistakes in films and then read the gapped sentences.","Your task is to fill the gaps with one or two words only according to the information in the article."],"title":"Cut! It’s another blunder on set","body":["It has been branded the funniest foul-up in Hollywood blockbuster history. In the first Star Wars film, evil stormtroopers break into a control room where the heroes are holed up. But if you watch closely, one soldier coming through the doorway bangs his head so hard he almost knocks himself out.","The incident has topped a new poll of movie blunders. The mistakes on the list, compiled by DVD rental firm Silverscreen, are a mixture of glaring continuity errors and on- camera blunders.","The advent of DVD players, which allow viewers to pause films frame by frame, has boosted the spotting of celluloid howlers.","In second place behind Star Wars is Commando, starring Arnold Schwarzenegger as an ex-special forces soldier apparently immune to bullets. He completely destroys one side of his yellow Porsche – yet moments later he is seen driving away in a pristine vehicle.","At No 3 is a gaffe in Ridley Scott’s Gladiator which reveals a production member in blue jeans standing behind Russell Crowe who is dressed in Roman regalia.","In fourth place is Charlie’s Angels. During one of the fight scenes, star Drew Barrymore tries to get Lucy Liu’s attention by calling out “Lucy” even though her character’s name is Alex.","Fifth is the Matrix. While Neo, played by Keanu Reeves, is being interrogated by Agent Smith his mouth is sealed. However, when the camera focuses on Smith his glasses show a reflection of Neo sitting down completely unharmed.","In sixth place comes Spider Man. Two muggers are thrown through two windows, but shortly afterwards the windows are intact.","Seventh is Terminator 3 – Rise of the Machines. While John and Catherine are in the aircraft hangar the tail number on the Cessna is N3035C. In the air the number shown is N9373F and when it lands it goes back to N3035C.","A No 8 is Harry Potter and the Philosopher’s Stone. After end-of-year exams Harry, Ron and Hermione rush to Hagrid. One of Harry’s lines finishes with, “Why didn’t I see it before?” But Hermione is behind him mouthing the lines.","Ninth is Black Hawk Down. When a Humvee pulls up to let someone cross the street viewers can see one of the crew members driving the car wearing a white T-shirt. But all the people who got into the car were wearing fatigues.","And last at No10 is The Rocky Horror Picture Show. While a criminologist talks about an event he describes it as “a late November evening”. However, later on, Brad and Janet are driving with the radio on and US President Nixon’s resignation is being broadcast. Nixon resigned in August 1974.","In the first line of the article the word {{0}} is a synonym for blunder or mistake.","In a George Lucas film a soldier hurts {{21}} instead of the enemy.","In the first four paragraphs of the article one more synonym for blunders, foul-ups, mistakes or errors is {{22}}.","After the crash in Commando, the hero’s {{23}} shouldn’t be seen in perfect condition.","In this historical film, viewers shouldn’t be able to see the {{24}} of one of the staff.","In Charlie’s Angels the actress’s {{25}} shouldn’t be heard.","A mistake in the interrogation scene in The Matrix means the viewers can see that the hero is {{26}}.","The windows should have been {{27}} after this incident in Spider Man.","In Terminator 3 it looks as if John and Catherine had got into a different {{28}} while they were in midair.","In a scene in The Philosopher’s Stone you can hear Harry Potter speaking, and at the same time you can also read the words on {{29}} lips.","In Black Hawk Down it is a staff member’s {{30}} that gives him away."],"grading":{"spelling":"lenient","caseSensitive":false},"items":[{"n":0,"example":true,"accept":["foul-up"]},{"n":21,"accept":["himself","his head"]},{"n":22,"accept":["howlers","howler"]},{"n":23,"accept":["car","yellow Porsche","Porsche"]},{"n":24,"accept":["blue jeans","jeans","trousers","clothes"]},{"n":25,"accept":["real name"]},{"n":26,"accept":["unharmed","OK"]},{"n":27,"accept":["broken","smashed"]},{"n":28,"accept":["aeroplane","plane","airplane"]},{"n":29,"accept":["Hermione’s"]},{"n":30,"accept":["white T-shirt","T-shirt"]}]}$mtr$::jsonb) on conflict (task_id) do update set task = excluded.task;
insert into public.tasks (id, exam_id, section, number, kind, exam_type, points, position, content, audio) values ($mtr$2006-febr-kozep-L2$mtr$, $mtr$2006-febr-kozep$mtr$, $mtr$language$mtr$, 2, $mtr$bank$mtr$, $mtr$szóbank (szavak visszahelyezése)$mtr$, 11, 5, $mtr${"id":"2006-febr-kozep-L2","number":2,"kind":"bank","layout":"inline","examType":"szóbank (szavak visszahelyezése)","points":11,"instructions":["You are going to read an article about a burglar. Some words are missing from the text.","Your task is to choose the most appropriate word from the list (A-N) for each gap (6-16) in the text. Write the letter of the appropriate word in the white box.","There is one extra word that you do not need to use."],"title":"BURGLAR MAKES NICE PROFIT","body":["An enterprising Norwegian found a way to make a nice profit by renting out an apartment in a {{0}} part of Oslo. What the renters didn’t know was {{6}} the 29-year-old man, whose name {{7}} not been released, had broken into someone {{8}} apartment and rented it out to 11 different people.","The police said the man {{9}} breaking into the apartment and posting its photographs on an Internet real estate site. He then asked {{10}} a bargain €780 per month in rent.","Since {{11}} an apartment normally costs 35 percent more in Oslo, his advertisement attracted more {{12}} 60 people. Eleven people were so {{13}} to rent the space that they each paid a €2,340 deposit. A total of €25,740 {{14}} transferred to the swindler’s bank account. The real renter was travelling at the time and has now {{15}} all the locks.","Ingrid Christiansen, of the Oslo police, said that the money was {{16}} in the suspect’s bank account and he would face fraud charges."],"bank":[{"key":"A","text":"admitted"},{"key":"B","text":"changed"},{"key":"C","text":"eager"},{"key":"D","text":"else’s"},{"key":"E","text":"for"},{"key":"F","text":"found"},{"key":"G","text":"has"},{"key":"H","text":"other’s"},{"key":"I","text":"popular"},{"key":"K","text":"such"},{"key":"L","text":"than"},{"key":"M","text":"that"},{"key":"N","text":"was"}],"items":[{"n":0,"example":true,"answer":"I"},{"n":6},{"n":7},{"n":8},{"n":9},{"n":10},{"n":11},{"n":12},{"n":13},{"n":14},{"n":15},{"n":16}]}$mtr$::jsonb, null)
insert into public.task_keys (task_id, task) values ($mtr$2006-febr-kozep-L2$mtr$, $mtr${"id":"2006-febr-kozep-L2","number":2,"kind":"bank","layout":"inline","examType":"szóbank (szavak visszahelyezése)","points":11,"instructions":["You are going to read an article about a burglar. Some words are missing from the text.","Your task is to choose the most appropriate word from the list (A-N) for each gap (6-16) in the text. Write the letter of the appropriate word in the white box.","There is one extra word that you do not need to use."],"title":"BURGLAR MAKES NICE PROFIT","body":["An enterprising Norwegian found a way to make a nice profit by renting out an apartment in a {{0}} part of Oslo. What the renters didn’t know was {{6}} the 29-year-old man, whose name {{7}} not been released, had broken into someone {{8}} apartment and rented it out to 11 different people.","The police said the man {{9}} breaking into the apartment and posting its photographs on an Internet real estate site. He then asked {{10}} a bargain €780 per month in rent.","Since {{11}} an apartment normally costs 35 percent more in Oslo, his advertisement attracted more {{12}} 60 people. Eleven people were so {{13}} to rent the space that they each paid a €2,340 deposit. A total of €25,740 {{14}} transferred to the swindler’s bank account. The real renter was travelling at the time and has now {{15}} all the locks.","Ingrid Christiansen, of the Oslo police, said that the money was {{16}} in the suspect’s bank account and he would face fraud charges."],"bank":[{"key":"A","text":"admitted"},{"key":"B","text":"changed"},{"key":"C","text":"eager"},{"key":"D","text":"else’s"},{"key":"E","text":"for"},{"key":"F","text":"found"},{"key":"G","text":"has"},{"key":"H","text":"other’s"},{"key":"I","text":"popular"},{"key":"K","text":"such"},{"key":"L","text":"than"},{"key":"M","text":"that"},{"key":"N","text":"was"}],"items":[{"n":0,"example":true,"answer":"I"},{"n":6,"answer":"M"},{"n":7,"answer":"G"},{"n":8,"answer":"D"},{"n":9,"answer":"A"},{"n":10,"answer":"E"},{"n":11,"answer":"K"},{"n":12,"answer":"L"},{"n":13,"answer":"C"},{"n":14,"answer":"N"},{"n":15,"answer":"B"},{"n":16,"answer":"F"}]}$mtr$::jsonb) on conflict (task_id) do update set task = excluded.task;
insert into public.tasks (id, exam_id, section, number, kind, exam_type, points, position, content, audio) values ($mtr$2006-febr-kozep-L3$mtr$, $mtr$2006-febr-kozep$mtr$, $mtr$language$mtr$, 3, $mtr$text$mtr$, $mtr$szóképzés (zárójeles szó)$mtr$, 9, 6, $mtr${"id":"2006-febr-kozep-L3","number":3,"kind":"text","layout":"inline","examType":"szóképzés (zárójeles szó)","points":9,"instructions":["You are going to read an article about sunbathing. Some words are missing from the text.","Use the words in brackets to form the words that fit in the gaps (17-25).","There might be cases when you do not have to change the word in brackets.","Use only one word for each gap."],"title":"THE TWO TOP SUNTAN MYTHS","body":["Everything about the sun is bad for you We hear so much about how {{0}} UV rays are that you’d be forgiven for thinking that {{17}} indoors all summer was good for you! But there are plenty of {{18}} things about being out in the sunshine too. A 15-minute {{19}} stroll in the sun will provide enough vitamin D to build strong bones. This vitamin also boosts the immune system, preventing infections such as colds. {{20}} days also help increase the level of a brain chemical called serotonin, which puts you in a good mood. If you are {{21}} enough (avoiding the hottest times of the day and using the appropriate sunscreen), the sun can actually help you get rid of some skin problems as well.","One bottle of sunscreen will be enough for the two of you on a 10-day holiday Not if you apply the amount used during testing in laboratories to achieve the level of {{22}} stated on the bottle. Experts say you should take one 400ml bottle of sunscreen per person for every 10 days of your holiday. Sunscreen should be applied 15 minutes before going out in the sun and then reapplied {{23}} and always after swimming. If you are using a spray, your skin should be completely {{24}} before you rub it in. And don’t forget the {{25}} places such as the soles of your feet and behind your ears."],"grading":{"spelling":"strict"},"items":[{"n":0,"prompt":"danger","example":true,"accept":["dangerous"]},{"n":17,"prompt":"stay"},{"n":18,"prompt":"use"},{"n":19,"prompt":"day"},{"n":20,"prompt":"sun"},{"n":21,"prompt":"careful"},{"n":22,"prompt":"protect"},{"n":23,"prompt":"frequent"},{"n":24,"prompt":"cover"},{"n":25,"prompt":"hide"}]}$mtr$::jsonb, null)
insert into public.task_keys (task_id, task) values ($mtr$2006-febr-kozep-L3$mtr$, $mtr${"id":"2006-febr-kozep-L3","number":3,"kind":"text","layout":"inline","examType":"szóképzés (zárójeles szó)","points":9,"instructions":["You are going to read an article about sunbathing. Some words are missing from the text.","Use the words in brackets to form the words that fit in the gaps (17-25).","There might be cases when you do not have to change the word in brackets.","Use only one word for each gap."],"title":"THE TWO TOP SUNTAN MYTHS","body":["Everything about the sun is bad for you We hear so much about how {{0}} UV rays are that you’d be forgiven for thinking that {{17}} indoors all summer was good for you! But there are plenty of {{18}} things about being out in the sunshine too. A 15-minute {{19}} stroll in the sun will provide enough vitamin D to build strong bones. This vitamin also boosts the immune system, preventing infections such as colds. {{20}} days also help increase the level of a brain chemical called serotonin, which puts you in a good mood. If you are {{21}} enough (avoiding the hottest times of the day and using the appropriate sunscreen), the sun can actually help you get rid of some skin problems as well.","One bottle of sunscreen will be enough for the two of you on a 10-day holiday Not if you apply the amount used during testing in laboratories to achieve the level of {{22}} stated on the bottle. Experts say you should take one 400ml bottle of sunscreen per person for every 10 days of your holiday. Sunscreen should be applied 15 minutes before going out in the sun and then reapplied {{23}} and always after swimming. If you are using a spray, your skin should be completely {{24}} before you rub it in. And don’t forget the {{25}} places such as the soles of your feet and behind your ears."],"grading":{"spelling":"strict","maxWords":1},"items":[{"n":0,"prompt":"danger","example":true,"accept":["dangerous"]},{"n":17,"prompt":"stay","accept":["staying"