 to acquire territory by performing stunts dictated by the game at public locations around the city, such as playing hopscotch at a crossroads while holding a hot-dog. \"People are more reserved than you would imagine,\" says Chang. Some players took to performing their stunt on rooftops to avoid being seen, she says, while others relished being ostentatious - like players of Pac-Manhattan, in which New Yorkers dress up as the video game icon Pac-Man and flee other gamers dressed up as ghosts.","Soon you may even be able to play games using phones without GPS hardware. One being played by 30,000 people in Sweden, Russia, Ireland, Finland and now China is called BotFighters, a role-playing game in which players explore an arena - in this case a city. Stumble into another player's territory, and you have to fight them by exchanging virtual blows boosted by acquired superpowers. Each blow is sent via a text message. The game exploits the location-based services provided by cellphone companies, where the position of each phone is tracked by its network. As location-based services become ever more sophisticated and accurate, so will the games."],"options":[{"key":"A","text":"TRUE"},{"key":"B","text":"FALSE"},{"key":"C","text":"NOT ENOUGH INFORMATION"}],"items":[{"n":"0a","example":true,"stem":"Matt carries several electronic gadgets while trying to find Uncle Roy.","answer":"B"},{"n":"0b","example":true,"stem":"The woman in black is going to tell him how the game continues.","answer":"C"},{"n":24,"stem":"A very large number of people in Britain have already tried games like Uncle Roy All Around You.","answer":"B"},{"n":25,"stem":"People who like spending a lot of time in front of the TV are no longer the only ones who play computer games.","answer":"A"},{"n":26,"stem":"Players in urban games can even take the part of famous people.","answer":"A"},{"n":27,"stem":"Many urban games like Digital Street Game are produced by Intel.","answer":"C"},{"n":28,"stem":"In Digital Street Game all players are happy to do their acts in the middle of the street.","answer":"B"},{"n":29,"stem":"BotFighters will be available in Hungary from next year.","answer":"C"},{"n":30,"stem":"Thanks to mobile technology urban games are now as highly developed as they will ever be.","answer":"B"}]}$mtr$::jsonb) on conflict (task_id) do update set task = excluded.task;
insert into public.tasks (id, exam_id, section, number, kind, exam_type, points, position, content, audio) values ($mtr$2006-okt-emelt-L1$mtr$, $mtr$2006-okt-emelt$mtr$, $mtr$language$mtr$, 1, $mtr$choice$mtr$, $mtr$feleletválasztós szövegkiegészítés (A-D)$mtr$, 9, 5, $mtr${"id":"2006-okt-emelt-L1","number":1,"kind":"choice","layout":"inline","examType":"feleletválasztós szövegkiegészítés (A-D)","points":9,"instructions":["You are going to read some advice on first dates. Some words are missing from the text.","Choose the most appropriate option (A-D) for each gap (1-9) in the text."],"title":"FIRST DATE CONVERSATION","body":["First dates are often seen as nerve-racking experiences. Plan in advance and {{0}} a few of our tips to banish the butterflies and sweaty palms.","You’ve done the hard work – you’ve approached {{1}} and not only talked to them but secured their telephone number and agreed to meet. So now comes the date itself. There’s {{2}} you can do to prepare.","The first thing to think about is {{3}} place to go. Lunch in a restaurant is a good option; it usually lasts between one and two hours and {{4}} no pressure to stick around if things don’t work out.","To take the pressure off the date you can prepare a loose plan of {{5}} you’d like to talk about. People are often panicked by awkward silences, but {{6}} preparation goes a long way. By reading a couple of newspapers to brush up on {{7}} affairs you will have plenty of material to keep your companion engaged. It {{8}} help to pick four or five interesting topics and jot them down. Nine times out of ten just {{9}} that they are there is enough – you’ll probably find that you don’t need them anyway.","So remember to prepare for yourself a conversational beginning, and now… put your dating skills to the test!"],"items":[{"n":0,"options":[{"key":"A","text":"attend"},{"key":"B","text":"apply"},{"key":"C","text":"approve"},{"key":"D","text":"admit"}],"example":true,"answer":"B"},{"n":1,"options":[{"key":"A","text":"someone"},{"key":"B","text":"anyone"},{"key":"C","text":"everyone"},{"key":"D","text":"no one"}]},{"n":2,"options":[{"key":"A","text":"lot"},{"key":"B","text":"lot of"},{"key":"C","text":"a lot"},{"key":"D","text":"lots of"}]},{"n":3,"options":[{"key":"A","text":"the better"},{"key":"B","text":"the good"},{"key":"C","text":"the best"},{"key":"D","text":"the nice"}]},{"n":4,"options":[{"key":"A","text":"it is"},{"key":"B","text":"there is"},{"key":"C","text":"there has"},{"key":"D","text":"it has"}]},{"n":5,"options":[{"key":"A","text":"how"},{"key":"B","text":"that"},{"key":"C","text":"which"},{"key":"D","text":"what"}]},{"n":6,"options":[{"key":"A","text":"a little"},{"key":"B","text":"little"},{"key":"C","text":"a bit"},{"key":"D","text":"a little bit"}]},{"n":7,"options":[{"key":"A","text":"actual"},{"key":"B","text":"currency"},{"key":"C","text":"active"},{"key":"D","text":"current"}]},{"n":8,"options":[{"key":"A","text":"has"},{"key":"B","text":"is about"},{"key":"C","text":"might"},{"key":"D","text":"needs"}]},{"n":9,"options":[{"key":"A","text":"know"},{"key":"B","text":"knowing"},{"key":"C","text":"having known"},{"key":"D","text":"known"}]}]}$mtr$::jsonb, null)
insert into public.task_keys (task_id, task) values ($mtr$2006-okt-emelt-L1$mtr$, $mtr${"id":"2006-okt-emelt-L1","number":1,"kind":"choice","layout":"inline","examType":"feleletválasztós szövegkiegészítés (A-D)","points":9,"instructions":["You are going to read some advice on first dates. Some words are missing from the text.","Choose the most appropriate option (A-D) for each gap (1-9) in the text."],"title":"FIRST DATE CONVERSATION","body":["First dates are often seen as nerve-racking experiences. Plan in advance and {{0}} a few of our tips to banish the butterflies and sweaty palms.","You’ve done the hard work – you’ve approached {{1}} and not only talked to them but secured their telephone number and agreed to meet. So now comes the date itself. There’s {{2}} you can do to prepare.","The first thing to think about is {{3}} place to go. Lunch in a restaurant is a good option; it usually lasts between one and two hours and {{4}} no pressure to stick around if things don’t work out.","To take the pressure off the date you can prepare a loose plan of {{5}} you’d like to talk about. People are often panicked by awkward silences, but {{6}} preparation goes a long way. By reading a couple of newspapers to brush up on {{7}} affairs you will have plenty of material to keep your companion engaged. It {{8}} help to pick four or five interesting topics and jot them down. Nine times out of ten just {{9}} that they are there is enough – you’ll probably find that you don’t need them anyway.","So remember to prepare for yourself a conversational beginning, and now… put your dating skills to the test!"],"items":[{"n":0,"options":[{"key":"A","text":"attend"},{"key":"B","text":"apply"},{"key":"C","text":"approve"},{"key":"D","text":"admit"}],"example":true,"answer":"B"},{"n":1,"options":[{"key":"A","text":"someone"},{"key":"B","text":"anyone"},{"key":"C","text":"everyone"},{"key":"D","text":"no one"}],"answer":"A"},{"n":2,"options":[{"key":"A","text":"lot"},{"key":"B","text":"lot of"},{"key":"C","text":"a lot"},{"key":"D","text":"lots of"}],"answer":"C"},{"n":3,"options":[{"key":"A","text":"the better"},{"key":"B","text":"the good"},{"key":"C","text":"the best"},{"key":"D","text":"the nice"}],"answer":"C"},{"n":4,"options":[{"key":"A","text":"it is"},{"key":"B","text":"there is"},{"key":"C","text":"there has"},{"key":"D","text":"it has"}],"answer":"B"},{"n":5,"options":[{"key":"A","text":"how"},{"key":"B","text":"that"},{"key":"C","text":"which"},{"key":"D","text":"what"}],"answer":"D"},{"n":6,"options":[{"key":"A","text":"a little"},{"key":"B","text":"little"},{"key":"C","text":"a bit"},{"key":"D","text":"a little bit"}],"answer":"A"},{"n":7,"options":[{"key":"A","text":"actual"},{"key":"B","text":"currency"},{"key":"C","text":"active"},{"key":"D","text":"current"}],"answer":"D"},{"n":8,"options":[{"key":"A","text":"has"},{"key":"B","text":"is about"},{"key":"C","text":"might"},{"key":"D","text":"needs"}],"answer":"C"},{"n":9,"options":[{"key":"A","text":"know"},{"key":"B","text":"knowing"},{"key":"C","text":"having known"},{"key":"D","text":"known"}],"answer":"B"}]}$mtr$::jsonb) on conflict (task_id) do update set task = excluded.task;
insert into public.tasks (id, exam_id, section, number, kind, exam_type, points, position, content, audio) values ($mtr$2006-okt-emelt-L2$mtr$, $mtr$2006-okt-emelt$mtr$, $mtr$language$mtr$, 2, $mtr$text$mtr$, $mtr$nyílt cloze (egy szó)$mtr$, 10, 6, $mtr${"id":"2006-okt-emelt-L2","number":2,"kind":"text","layout":"inline","examType":"nyílt cloze (egy szó)","points":10,"instructions":["You are going to read an article about family meals. Some words are missing from the text.","Your task is to write the missing words - one word for each gap - on the dotted lines (10-19) after the text."],"title":"TABLE MANNERS","body":["After hooded tops, the disappearance of family meals is the latest thing turning youngsters into yobbos, {{0}} to British politicians. The government has promised to create a ‘culture of respect’, and getting more families {{10}} eat together is a good start.","Parenting experts warn of a growing number of TV dinner toddlers unable to {{11}} a knife and fork, and isolated teenagers who take their meals from the freezer to the microwave and up to the bedroom {{12}} a word to anyone. All because many families no {{13}} eat together.","According to a national survey, 20% of {{14}} asked sat down to eat together just once a week. The poll, by parenting organisation Raisingkids, found children often had meals alone in their bedrooms {{15}} watching TV or playing computer games. Of those {{16}} did eat together, TV was the preferred dinner guest.","Child psychologist Dr Pat Spungin says, the benefits of family meals are far-reaching and should {{17}} be underestimated. The organisation is running a ‘Back to table’ campaign {{18}} get families eating together again. “Family meals give confidence and teach children {{19}} to behave with others,” says Dr Spungin. “This isn’t only in the home but in the outside world as well.”"],"grading":{"spelling":"strict"},"items":[{"n":0,"example":true,"accept":["according"]},{"n":10},{"n":11},{"n":12},{"n":13},{"n":14},{"n":15},{"n":16},{"n":17},{"n":18},{"n":19}]}$mtr$::jsonb, null)
insert into public.task_keys (task_id, task) values ($mtr$2006-okt-emelt-L2$mtr$, $mtr${"id":"2006-okt-emelt-L2","number":2,"kind":"text","layout":"inline","examType":"nyílt cloze (egy szó)","points":10,"instructions":["You are going to read an article about family meals. Some words are missing from the text.","Your task is to write the missing words - one word for each gap - on the dotted lines (10-19) after the text."],"title":"TABLE MANNERS","body":["After hooded tops, the disappearance of family meals is the latest thing turning youngsters into yobbos, {{0}} to British politicians. The government has promised to create a ‘culture of respect’, and getting more families {{10}} eat together is a good start.","Parenting experts warn of a growing number of TV dinner toddlers unable to {{11}} a knife and fork, and isolated teenagers who take their meals from the freezer to the microwave and up to the bedroom {{12}} a word to anyone. All because many families no {{13}} eat together.","According to a national survey, 20% of {{14}} asked sat down to eat together just once a week. The poll, by parenting organisation Raisingkids, found children often had meals alone in their bedrooms {{15}} watching TV or playing computer games. Of those {{16}} did eat together, TV was the preferred dinner guest.","Child psychologist Dr Pat Spungin says, the benefits of family meals are far-reaching and should {{17}} be underestimated. The organisation is running a ‘Back to table’ campaign {{18}} get families eating together again. “Family meals give confidence and teach children {{19}} to behave with others,” says Dr Spungin. “This isn’t only in the home but in the outside world as well.”"],"grading":{"spelling":"strict","maxWords":1},"items":[{"n":0,"example":true,"accept":["according"]},{"n":10,"accept":["to"]},{"n":11,"accept":["use","hold","handle","manage"]},{"n":12,"accept":["without"]},{"n":13,"accept":["longer"]},{"n":14,"accept":["those","people","families"]},{"n":15,"accept":["while","when"]},{"n":16,"accept":["who","that"]},{"n":17,"accept":["not"]},{"n":18,"accept":["to"]},{"n":19,"accept":["how"]}]}$mtr$::jsonb) on conflict (task_id) do update set task = excluded.task;
insert into public.tasks (id, exam_id, section, number, kind, exam_type, points, position, content, audio) values ($mtr$2006-okt-emelt-L3$mtr$, $mtr$2006-okt-emelt$mtr$, $mtr$language$mtr$, 3, $mtr$text$mtr$, $mtr$szóképzés (zárójeles szó)$mtr$, 8, 7, $mtr${"id":"2006-okt-emelt-L3","number":3,"kind":"text","layout":"inline","examType":"szóképzés (zárójeles szó)","points":8,"instructions":["You are going to read an invitation for a story-telling competition. Some words are missing from the text.","Use the words in brackets to form the words that fit in the gaps (20-27).","There might be cases when you do not have to change the word in brackets.","Use one word for each gap."],"title":"ONCE UPON A TIME","body":["Ever wanted to tell an amazing story, but didn’t know where to start? Or have you already started writing {{0}} and original stories that you now want to set free? It doesn’t matter whether you’re at the top of your class at English or not – we’re {{20}} in stories with a spark, whether they’re funny or sad, set in a {{21}} universe or based on real-life events.","There are plenty of chances to shine, as we’ll choose ten winners {{22}} into three age groups: under-8s, 9-11, and those aged 12 and over. The winners will help {{23}} their words into exciting radio at BBC studios, and the stories will be {{24}} on a BBC 7 radio show.","Want a bit of {{25}}? BBC 7’s {{26}} show has a story every day which could help spark an idea. If you wish to enter, you can send your story {{27}} typed or printed, along with an entry form. Stories will be judged on the basis of their originality of plot and characterisation."],"grading":{"spelling":"strict"},"items":[{"n":0,"prompt":"imagine","example":true,"accept":["imaginative"]},{"n":20,"prompt":"interest"},{"n":21,"prompt":"fantasy"},{"n":22,"prompt":"separate"},{"n":23,"prompt":"transform"},{"n":24,"prompt":"broadcast"},{"n":25,"prompt":"inspire"},{"n":26,"prompt":"interact"},{"n":27,"prompt":"prefer"}]}$mtr$::jsonb, null)
insert into public.task_keys (task_id, task) values ($mtr$2006-okt-emelt-L3$mtr$, $mtr${"id":"2006-okt-emelt-L3","number":3,"kind":"text","layout":"inline","examType":"szóképzés (zárójeles szó)","points":8,"instructions":["You are going to read an invitation for a story-telling competition. Some words are missing from the text.","Use the words in brackets to form the words that fit in the gaps (20-27).","There might be cases when you do not have to change the word in brackets.","Use one word for each gap."],"title":"ONCE UPON A TIME","body":["Ever wanted to tell an amazing story, but didn’t know where to start? Or have you already started writing {{0}} and original stories that you now want to set free? It doesn’t matter whether you’re at the top of your class at English or not – we’re {{20}} in stories with a spark, whether they’re funny or sad, set in a {{21}} universe or based on real-life events.","There are plenty of chances to shine, as we’ll choose ten winners {{22}} into three age groups: under-8s, 9-11, and those aged 12 and over. The winners will help {{23}} their words into exciting radio at BBC studios, and the stories will be {{24}} on a BBC 7 radio show.","Want a bit of {{25}}? BBC 7’s {{26}} show has a story every day which could help spark an idea. If you wish to enter, you can send your story {{27}} typed or printed, along with an entry form. Stories will be judged on the basis of their originality of plot and characterisation."],"grading":{"spelling":"strict","maxWords":1},"items":[{"n":0,"prompt":"imagine","example":true,"accept":["imaginative"]},{"n":20,"prompt":"interest","accept":["interested"]},{"n":21,"prompt":"fantasy","accept":["fantasy","fantastic","fantastical"]},{"n":22,"prompt":"separate","accept":["separated"]},{"n":23,"prompt":"transform","accept":["transform"]},{"n":24,"prompt":"broadcast","accept":["broadcast","broadcasted"]},{"n":25,"prompt":"inspire","accept":["inspiration"]},{"n":26,"prompt":"interact","accept":["interactive"]},{"n":27,"prompt":"prefer","accept":["preferably"]}]}$mtr$::jsonb) on conflict (task_id) do update set task = excluded.task;
insert into public.tasks (id, exam_id, section, number, kind, exam_type, points, position, content, audio) values ($mtr$2006-okt-emelt-L4$mtr$, $mtr$2006-okt-emelt$mtr$, $mtr$language$mtr$, 4, $mtr$lines$mtr$, $mtr$soronkénti hibakeresés (felesleges szó vagy helyes sor)$mtr$, 13, 8, $mtr${"id":"2006-okt-emelt-L4","number":4,"kind":"lines","layout":"lines","examType":"soronkénti hibakeresés (felesleges szó vagy helyes sor)","points":13,"instructions":["You are going to read an article about being confident. In most lines there is one word that should not be there. It is either grammatically incorrect or does not fit in with the sense of the text.","Read the text and then copy the extra word in the space provided after each line.","Some lines are correct. Indicate these lines with a tick (9).","The task begins with two examples (0)."],"title":"GET CONFIDENT","intro":"","items":[{"n":"0a","example":true,"text":"Everybody could neither do with a bit more confidence in one or","answer":"neither"},{"n":"0b","example":true,"text":"more areas of their lives, whether it’s at work, in a relationship or in","answer":null},{"n":28,"text":"meeting by new people. We can all feel under pressure to live up to"},{"n":29,"text":"ideals imposed on to us by our families, work colleagues, the media"},{"n":30,"text":"and even though ourselves. At times these goals are unrealistic. Such"},{"n":31,"text":"pressure can cause anxiety and bruise confidence."},{"n":32,"text":"The Oxford English Dictionary defines ‘confidence’ as if being self-"},{"n":33,"text":"assured and feeling or showing self-reliance. You have a whole range"},{"n":34,"text":"of strengths, skills and abilities available to you which will enhance"},{"n":35,"text":"your confidence with. But sometimes you may not be fully aware of"},{"n":36,"text":"all them. By becoming more aware of these tools and the ways in"},{"n":37,"text":"which you can apply from them in the face of life’s challenges, you"},{"n":38,"text":"can build your confidence. If you feel more is required of you than"},{"n":39,"text":"that you are able to give when faced with a challenge, you are likely"},{"n":40,"text":"to feel less in the control, more anxious, more helpless and stressed."}]}$mtr$::jsonb, null)
insert into public.task_keys (task_id, task) values ($mtr$2006-okt-emelt-L4$mtr$, $mtr${"id":"2006-okt-emelt-L4","number":4,"kind":"lines","layout":"lines","examType":"soronkénti hibakeresés (felesleges szó vagy helyes sor)","points":13,"instructions":["You are going to read an article about being confident. In most lines there is one word that should not be there. It is either grammatically incorrect or does not fit in with the sense of the text.","Read the text and then copy the extra word in the space provided after each line.","Some lines are correct. Indicate these lines with a tick (9).","The task begins with two examples (0)."],"title":"GET CONFIDENT","intro":"","items":[{"n":"0a","example":true,"text":"Everybody could neither do with a bit more confidence in one or","answer":"neither"},{"n":"0b","example":true,"text":"more areas of their lives, whether it’s at work, in a relationship or in","answer":null},{"n":28,"text":"meeting by new people. We can all feel under pressure to live up to","answer":"by"},{"n":29,"text":"ideals imposed on to us by our families, work colleagues, the media","answer":"to"},{"n":30,"text":"and even though ourselves. At times these goals are unrealistic. Such","answer":"though"},{"n":31,"text":"pressure can cause anxiety and bruise confidence.","answer":null},{"n":32,"text":"The Oxford English Dictionary defines ‘confidence’ as if being self-","answer":"if"},{"n":33,"text":"assured and feeling or showing self-reliance. You have a whole range","answer":null},{"n":34,"text":"of strengths, skills and abilities available to you which will enhance","answer":null},{"n":35,"text":"your confidence with. But sometimes you may not be fully aware of","answer":"with"},{"n":36,"text":"all them. By becoming more aware of these tools and the ways in","answer":"all"},{"n":37,"text":"which you can apply from them in the face of life’s challenges, you","answer":"from"},{"n":38,"text":"can build your confidence. If you feel more is required of you than","answer":null},{"n":39,"text":"that you are able to give when faced with a challenge, you are likely","answer":"that"},{"n":40,"text":"to feel less in the control, more anxious, more helpless and stressed.","answer":"the"}]}$mtr$::jsonb) on conflict (task_id) do update set task = excluded.task;
insert into public.tasks (id, exam_id, section, number, kind, exam_type, points, position, content, audio) values ($mtr$2006-okt-emelt-H1$mtr$, $mtr$2006-okt-emelt$mtr$, $mtr$listening$mtr$, 1, $mtr$choice$mtr$, $mtr$feleletválasztás hallás után$mtr$, 7, 9, $mtr${"id":"2006-okt-emelt-H1","number":1,"kind":"choice","layout":"stems","examType":"feleletválasztás hallás után","points":7,"instructions":["In this section, you are going to hear an interview with Brian, who is talking about New England and a traditional meal called a clambake.","Your task is to write the letter of the correct answer into the boxes on the right.","First, you will have some time to study the task, and then we will play the whole recording in one piece.","Then, after a short pause, you will hear the recording again, but this time we will play the text in shorter sections to give you enough time to write down your answers.","At the end, you will have some more time to check your work."],"audio":{"file":"e_angol_06okt_fl.mp3","start":0,"end":558.7,"clip":"hang/e_angol_06okt_fl_H1.mp3"},"items":[{"n":0,"example":true,"stem":"New England …","options":[{"key":"A","text":"consists of six states."},{"key":"B","text":"is a state in the northern part of the US."},{"key":"C","text":"is the sixth state in the United States."}],"answer":"A"},{"n":1,"stem":"Brian … a Yankee.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"doesn't like being called"},{"key":"B","text":"thinks of himself as"},{"key":"C","text":"would call everybody from the United States"}]},{"n":2,"stem":"A clambake is a …","options":[{"key":"A","text":"barbecue on the beach."},{"key":"B","text":"cookout in the garden."},{"key":"C","text":"cookout by the sea."}]},{"n":3,"stem":"Brian names … animals from the sea.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"two"},{"key":"B","text":"three"},{"key":"C","text":"four"}]},{"n":4,"stem":"On top of the clambake, there is …","options":[{"key":"A","text":"seaweed."},{"key":"B","text":"food."},{"key":"C","text":"sand."}]},{"n":5,"stem":"You steam the clambake for about … minutes.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"thirty"},{"key":"B","text":"sixty"},{"key":"C","text":"ninety"}]},{"n":6,"stem":"You don’t eat … of a lobster.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"all"},{"key":"B","text":"the claws"},{"key":"C","text":"the tail"}]},{"n":7,"stem":"When you start cooking a lobster, it is …","options":[{"key":"A","text":"white."},{"key":"B","text":"red."},{"key":"C","text":"greenish black."}]}]}$mtr$::jsonb, $mtr${"file":"e_angol_06okt_fl.mp3","start":0,"end":558.7,"clip":"hang/e_angol_06okt_fl_H1.mp3"}$mtr$::jsonb)
