y":"A","text":"the lower the fare you're likely to find."},{"key":"B","text":"it may cost less ultimately to book it for a full week."},{"key":"C","text":"when fares are more expensive."},{"key":"D","text":"the more expensive they are."},{"key":"E","text":"it's cheapest to fly on Tuesday, Wednesday and Saturday."},{"key":"F","text":"than if you extended your trip to Sunday morning."},{"key":"G","text":"and the discounted fare may be sold out by the next day."},{"key":"H","text":"so book your room at the same time as you make your travel plans."}],"items":[{"n":0,"example":true,"answer":"C"},{"n":10,"answer":"G"},{"n":11,"answer":"A"},{"n":12,"answer":"F"},{"n":13,"answer":"E"},{"n":14,"answer":"D"},{"n":15,"answer":"H"}]}$mtr$::jsonb) on conflict (task_id) do update set task = excluded.task;
insert into public.tasks (id, exam_id, section, number, kind, exam_type, points, position, content, audio) values ($mtr$2007-maj-kozep-R3$mtr$, $mtr$2007-maj-kozep$mtr$, $mtr$reading$mtr$, 3, $mtr$bank$mtr$, $mtr$kérdés/cím párosítása bekezdéshez$mtr$, 8, 3, $mtr${"id":"2007-maj-kozep-R3","number":3,"kind":"bank","layout":"inline","examType":"kérdés/cím párosítása bekezdéshez","points":8,"instructions":["In the following interview with Chef Don Zajac the questions have been removed.","Your task is to read the text and match the questions with the answers.","There is one extra question that you do not need."],"body":["{{0}}\nYes, coming from a Polish family with a history of being in the business, it was natural to prepare meals.","{{16}}\nPassion and desire. When I was growing up, my folks always wanted me to be happy at what I did for a living. \"You'll work for the remainder of your life, so be happy with what you choose.\"","{{17}}\nI had a passion for what I wanted so the learning came very easy. I went to Joliet Junior College, which had a Culinary Arts Program. The school was pretty tough.","{{18}}\nKnow your limitations and build your skills slowly. Quality, passion and love must go into everything you do.","{{19}}\nA K-5 Kitchen Aid, which is a 5-quart mixer. This piece of equipment is very convenient and valuable.","{{20}}\nNever skimp on quality ingredients. Cook with what you drink. Never be afraid to ask questions.","{{21}}\nWell it really wasn't funny then, but one time a cook was lighting a pilot light and threw the lit piece of paper he was using to light the stove in the garbage can. The can caught fire in the middle of dinner.","{{22}}\nI love to use Pacific Sable when preparing a fish course. It has wonderful characteristics and is always pleasing.","{{23}}\nTwo books: one is Paul Bocuse's French Cooking, the other is Patés and Terrines.","Thanks for the interview, Chef Don."],"bank":[{"key":"A","text":"What's the funniest kitchen incident you can remember?"},{"key":"B","text":"What's your favorite gadget?"},{"key":"C","text":"What's your favorite food to cook with?"},{"key":"D","text":"Do you often cook Polish food?"},{"key":"E","text":"What made you decide you would become a professional cook?"},{"key":"F","text":"What's your best cooking tip for a beginner?"},{"key":"G","text":"What's your favorite cookbook?"},{"key":"H","text":"What's the best piece of advice you would give a home enthusiast?"},{"key":"I","text":"Where were you trained and how difficult was your training?"},{"key":"J","text":"Chef, did you cook when you were growing up?"}],"items":[{"n":0,"example":true,"answer":"J"},{"n":16},{"n":17},{"n":18},{"n":19},{"n":20},{"n":21},{"n":22},{"n":23}]}$mtr$::jsonb, null)
insert into public.task_keys (task_id, task) values ($mtr$2007-maj-kozep-R3$mtr$, $mtr${"id":"2007-maj-kozep-R3","number":3,"kind":"bank","layout":"inline","examType":"kérdés/cím párosítása bekezdéshez","points":8,"instructions":["In the following interview with Chef Don Zajac the questions have been removed.","Your task is to read the text and match the questions with the answers.","There is one extra question that you do not need."],"body":["{{0}}\nYes, coming from a Polish family with a history of being in the business, it was natural to prepare meals.","{{16}}\nPassion and desire. When I was growing up, my folks always wanted me to be happy at what I did for a living. \"You'll work for the remainder of your life, so be happy with what you choose.\"","{{17}}\nI had a passion for what I wanted so the learning came very easy. I went to Joliet Junior College, which had a Culinary Arts Program. The school was pretty tough.","{{18}}\nKnow your limitations and build your skills slowly. Quality, passion and love must go into everything you do.","{{19}}\nA K-5 Kitchen Aid, which is a 5-quart mixer. This piece of equipment is very convenient and valuable.","{{20}}\nNever skimp on quality ingredients. Cook with what you drink. Never be afraid to ask questions.","{{21}}\nWell it really wasn't funny then, but one time a cook was lighting a pilot light and threw the lit piece of paper he was using to light the stove in the garbage can. The can caught fire in the middle of dinner.","{{22}}\nI love to use Pacific Sable when preparing a fish course. It has wonderful characteristics and is always pleasing.","{{23}}\nTwo books: one is Paul Bocuse's French Cooking, the other is Patés and Terrines.","Thanks for the interview, Chef Don."],"bank":[{"key":"A","text":"What's the funniest kitchen incident you can remember?"},{"key":"B","text":"What's your favorite gadget?"},{"key":"C","text":"What's your favorite food to cook with?"},{"key":"D","text":"Do you often cook Polish food?"},{"key":"E","text":"What made you decide you would become a professional cook?"},{"key":"F","text":"What's your best cooking tip for a beginner?"},{"key":"G","text":"What's your favorite cookbook?"},{"key":"H","text":"What's the best piece of advice you would give a home enthusiast?"},{"key":"I","text":"Where were you trained and how difficult was your training?"},{"key":"J","text":"Chef, did you cook when you were growing up?"}],"items":[{"n":0,"example":true,"answer":"J"},{"n":16,"answer":"E"},{"n":17,"answer":"I"},{"n":18,"answer":"F"},{"n":19,"answer":"B"},{"n":20,"answer":"H"},{"n":21,"answer":"A"},{"n":22,"answer":"C"},{"n":23,"answer":"G"}]}$mtr$::jsonb) on conflict (task_id) do update set task = excluded.task;
insert into public.tasks (id, exam_id, section, number, kind, exam_type, points, position, content, audio) values ($mtr$2007-maj-kozep-R4$mtr$, $mtr$2007-maj-kozep$mtr$, $mtr$reading$mtr$, 4, $mtr$choice$mtr$, $mtr$igaz / hamis / nincs elég információ (A/B/C)$mtr$, 7, 4, $mtr${"id":"2007-maj-kozep-R4","number":4,"kind":"choice","layout":"stems","examType":"igaz / hamis / nincs elég információ (A/B/C)","points":7,"instructions":["Read the following text and the statements following it.","Your task is to mark each statement","A if it says the same as the text,","B if it says something different from the text,","C if the text does not give enough information for you to choose A or B. Write the letters in the white boxes."],"title":"Question time","body":["There is a growing need to find answers to lots of different types of questions, and thousands of people are ready to pay for instant-reply services.","A company called Any Question Answered (AQA) offers an open-all-hours service, charging £1 for each question and responding to about 80% within five minutes. At present, the service is answering an average of 8,000 questions per day - with replies written by a team of 500 part-time researchers.","So what makes people want to use this pay-as-you-know service? The peak time for questions is the evening, around the time people might have had some alcohol. And AQA's chief executive, Colin Myers, says these are usually \"male type\" inquiries.","\"Some people want to tease their friends about what they don't know. Who won a football match? Who scored the most goals?\" \"There are other questions which are clearly about settling an argument. Such as 'If a polar bear and a lion had a fight who would win?' Definitely the polar bear. It can include more specific questions, such as \"Who should get the next round of drinks?\" And the fact that the questioners get a response from a human being, maybe with some humour added, means that people are using it as a form of instant entertainment, he says.","About a third of questions sent in by customers have already been asked, says Mr. Myers. And although some topics are excluded, such as medical or financial advice, the researchers try to answer whatever is thrown at them. \"What goes well with orange trousers?\" Answer: a purple satin shirt. If a customer thinks the answer is wrong or they think it's unsatisfactory, they can dispute it and ask for their money back.","AQA is a serious business which aims to give instant information to people on the move. Mr. Myers used to run a computer company and a mobile-phone technology firm. He believes the huge mobile phone market is providing rich opportunities for new services."],"options":[{"key":"A","text":"TRUE"},{"key":"B","text":"FALSE"},{"key":"C","text":"NOT ENOUGH INFORMATION"}],"items":[{"n":0,"example":true,"stem":"You get the answer in written form.","answer":"A"},{"n":24,"stem":"The service is available 24 hours a day."},{"n":25,"stem":"You must pay £1 for each answer."},{"n":26,"stem":"Everybody gets their answer within five minutes."},{"n":27,"stem":"Most of the questions are asked in the evening."},{"n":28,"stem":"The oldest person who called was eighty years old."},{"n":29,"stem":"Any kind of question is answered."},{"n":30,"stem":"Mr. Myers can speak five languages."}]}$mtr$::jsonb, null)
insert into public.task_keys (task_id, task) values ($mtr$2007-maj-kozep-R4$mtr$, $mtr${"id":"2007-maj-kozep-R4","number":4,"kind":"choice","layout":"stems","examType":"igaz / hamis / nincs elég információ (A/B/C)","points":7,"instructions":["Read the following text and the statements following it.","Your task is to mark each statement","A if it says the same as the text,","B if it says something different from the text,","C if the text does not give enough information for you to choose A or B. Write the letters in the white boxes."],"title":"Question time","body":["There is a growing need to find answers to lots of different types of questions, and thousands of people are ready to pay for instant-reply services.","A company called Any Question Answered (AQA) offers an open-all-hours service, charging £1 for each question and responding to about 80% within five minutes. At present, the service is answering an average of 8,000 questions per day - with replies written by a team of 500 part-time researchers.","So what makes people want to use this pay-as-you-know service? The peak time for questions is the evening, around the time people might have had some alcohol. And AQA's chief executive, Colin Myers, says these are usually \"male type\" inquiries.","\"Some people want to tease their friends about what they don't know. Who won a football match? Who scored the most goals?\" \"There are other questions which are clearly about settling an argument. Such as 'If a polar bear and a lion had a fight who would win?' Definitely the polar bear. It can include more specific questions, such as \"Who should get the next round of drinks?\" And the fact that the questioners get a response from a human being, maybe with some humour added, means that people are using it as a form of instant entertainment, he says.","About a third of questions sent in by customers have already been asked, says Mr. Myers. And although some topics are excluded, such as medical or financial advice, the researchers try to answer whatever is thrown at them. \"What goes well with orange trousers?\" Answer: a purple satin shirt. If a customer thinks the answer is wrong or they think it's unsatisfactory, they can dispute it and ask for their money back.","AQA is a serious business which aims to give instant information to people on the move. Mr. Myers used to run a computer company and a mobile-phone technology firm. He believes the huge mobile phone market is providing rich opportunities for new services."],"options":[{"key":"A","text":"TRUE"},{"key":"B","text":"FALSE"},{"key":"C","text":"NOT ENOUGH INFORMATION"}],"items":[{"n":0,"example":true,"stem":"You get the answer in written form.","answer":"A"},{"n":24,"stem":"The service is available 24 hours a day.","answer":"A"},{"n":25,"stem":"You must pay £1 for each answer.","answer":"B"},{"n":26,"stem":"Everybody gets their answer within five minutes.","answer":"B"},{"n":27,"stem":"Most of the questions are asked in the evening.","answer":"A"},{"n":28,"stem":"The oldest person who called was eighty years old.","answer":"C"},{"n":29,"stem":"Any kind of question is answered.","answer":"B"},{"n":30,"stem":"Mr. Myers can speak five languages.","answer":"C"}]}$mtr$::jsonb) on conflict (task_id) do update set task = excluded.task;
insert into public.tasks (id, exam_id, section, number, kind, exam_type, points, position, content, audio) values ($mtr$2007-maj-kozep-L1$mtr$, $mtr$2007-maj-kozep$mtr$, $mtr$language$mtr$, 1, $mtr$order$mtr$, $mtr$összekevert szavak mondattá rendezése$mtr$, 6, 5, $mtr${"id":"2007-maj-kozep-L1","number":1,"kind":"order","layout":"stems","examType":"összekevert szavak mondattá rendezése","points":6,"instructions":["The words in the sentences below are jumbled up.","Your task is to form the correct sentences and write them on the dotted lines. The first word is there for you.","You have to use each word.","Do not change the form of the words."],"items":[{"n":0,"first":"Next","words":["summer","we","London","going","are","visit","to"],"end":".","accept":[["summer","we","are","going","to","visit","London"]],"example":true},{"n":1,"first":"John","words":["to","was","home","it","started","walking","when","rain"],"end":"."},{"n":2,"first":"Tomorrow","words":["are","to","explore","the","going","we","island"],"end":"."},{"n":3,"first":"Could","words":["you","me","some","send","more","pictures"],"end":"?"},{"n":4,"first":"Carla","words":["clothes","likes","casual","wearing"],"end":"."},{"n":5,"first":"I","words":["because","ending","like","the","didn’t","film","it","a","had","sad"],"end":"."},{"n":6,"first":"The","words":["new","was","a","year","library","built","ago"],"end":"."}]}$mtr$::jsonb, null)
