rion True, a former Getty Museum antiquities curator and Robert Hecht, an American art dealer based in Paris. As a representative of the world’s richest art institution, True is accused of illegally obtaining 42 items during the 1980s and 1990s, including a 2,000-year statue of Apollo unearthed in Italy. The charges carry a 10-year sentence. She denies the charge − as does Hecht −and the Getty Museum says she is innocent.","Rocco Buttiglione, the Italian minister for culture, said Italy is paving the way for other countries to retrieve looted heritage. ‘The age of trafficking in art pieces is over,’ he warned.","The global trade in stolen art treasures is worth … billions… of pounds.","Rich {{17}} art collectors and museums play an important role in illicit art trade.","One case in France concerns an old {{18}}.","The person thought to be responsible for having stolen and sold it is called {{19}}.","According to Agnes Saal it should be returned to the {{20}}.","The aim of Colonel Roger Lembert and his {{21}} is to stop art smuggling.","If found guilty of art trafficking, Marion True will probably be sent to {{22}}.","The Italian Minister for Culture believes Italian efforts to get their art treasures back will make it easier for {{23}} to do so, too."],"grading":{"spelling":"lenient","caseSensitive":false},"items":[{"n":17,"accept":["American","US"]},{"n":18,"accept":["Hebrew manuscript","text","document","Hebrew text","Hebrew document","manuscript"]},{"n":19,"accept":["Michel Garel"]},{"n":20,"accept":["National Library"]},{"n":21,"accept":["police unit","30 men","team","men","police men","police team"]},{"n":22,"accept":["prison","gaol","jail"]},{"n":23,"accept":["other countries"]}]}$mtr$::jsonb) on conflict (task_id) do update set task = excluded.task;
insert into public.tasks (id, exam_id, section, number, kind, exam_type, points, position, content, audio) values ($mtr$2007-okt-emelt-R4$mtr$, $mtr$2007-okt-emelt$mtr$, $mtr$reading$mtr$, 4, $mtr$bank$mtr$, $mtr$sorba rendezés$mtr$, 5, 4, $mtr${"id":"2007-okt-emelt-R4","number":4,"kind":"bank","layout":"inline","examType":"sorba rendezés","points":5,"instructions":["In this story of a dramatic rescue operation at sea some paragraphs have been jumbled up.","Your task is to put them back in order.","Remember that there is an extra letter that you do not need."],"title":"Navy helicopter lifts lifeboat crew to safety in island yacht-rescue drama","body":["A lifeboat crew was saved by a Royal Navy helicopter yesterday when the would-be rescuers became victims of the sea themselves in an early morning air-sea rescue drama.","{{0}}\nBuffeted by rising winds and high seas, the pilot of the military helicopter managed to hover close enough to the reef to allow the three men to clamber aboard.","{{24}}\nLater yesterday, the man in charge of the Royal National Lifeboat Institution (RNLI) paid tribute to the helicopter crew for their crucial role in averting what could have been a disaster.","{{25}}\nThe drama began at 12:45am yesterday morning when a frantic call from a mobile phone alerted the Clyde Coastguard operations centre.","Minutes before, the 50ft motor yacht, Enterprise, crewed by two men, had run aground on a reef off the coast of Jura. As the vessel sank, one man managed to reach the relative security of the reef itself. His companion plunged into the sea and swam to a tiny island nearby.","{{26}}","{{27}}\nWearing night-vision goggles, the helicopter’s crew of five were able to pick out the stranded men because of the lifeboat men’s survival gear that shone like beacons.","Capt Hills said: “We couldn’t actually touch down because of the contour of the land and the bushes, but we held steady long enough to get everyone on board.","{{28}}"],"bank":[{"key":"A","text":"Michael Vlasto, the operations director of the RNLI, said: “We are very grateful to the Royal Navy for airlifting our two volunteer crewmen back on board the lifeboat, and getting the two yachtsmen safely to dry land.”"},{"key":"B","text":"When the lifeboat reached the scene, the captain realised he could not get his lifeboat close enough to the scene and launched the lifeboat’s inflatable vessel which filled with water and trapped the two lifeboat men along with the yachtsman on the reef. However, the Royal Navy Sea King helicopter was en route to the scene."},{"key":"C","text":"The two-man lifeboat crew became trapped on a sliver of reef along with a stranded yachtsman they had been attempting to rescue."},{"key":"D","text":"The hospital spokesman said: “They were feeling fine and have been discharged.”"},{"key":"E","text":"Once on land, he used his mobile phone to summon the rescue services."},{"key":"F","text":"It was a good operation; we got the other guy, too. Thankfully, all is well that ends well.”"},{"key":"G","text":"The pilot, Captain Ian Hills, then gingerly moved his Sea King helicopter toward a tiny island off the coast of Jura, in the Inner Hebrides, where he was able to pick up a second stranded yachtsman."}],"items":[{"n":0,"example":true,"answer":"C"},{"n":24},{"n":25},{"n":26},{"n":27},{"n":28}]}$mtr$::jsonb, null)
insert into public.task_keys (task_id, task) values ($mtr$2007-okt-emelt-R4$mtr$, $mtr${"id":"2007-okt-emelt-R4","number":4,"kind":"bank","layout":"inline","examType":"sorba rendezés","points":5,"instructions":["In this story of a dramatic rescue operation at sea some paragraphs have been jumbled up.","Your task is to put them back in order.","Remember that there is an extra letter that you do not need."],"title":"Navy helicopter lifts lifeboat crew to safety in island yacht-rescue drama","body":["A lifeboat crew was saved by a Royal Navy helicopter yesterday when the would-be rescuers became victims of the sea themselves in an early morning air-sea rescue drama.","{{0}}\nBuffeted by rising winds and high seas, the pilot of the military helicopter managed to hover close enough to the reef to allow the three men to clamber aboard.","{{24}}\nLater yesterday, the man in charge of the Royal National Lifeboat Institution (RNLI) paid tribute to the helicopter crew for their crucial role in averting what could have been a disaster.","{{25}}\nThe drama began at 12:45am yesterday morning when a frantic call from a mobile phone alerted the Clyde Coastguard operations centre.","Minutes before, the 50ft motor yacht, Enterprise, crewed by two men, had run aground on a reef off the coast of Jura. As the vessel sank, one man managed to reach the relative security of the reef itself. His companion plunged into the sea and swam to a tiny island nearby.","{{26}}","{{27}}\nWearing night-vision goggles, the helicopter’s crew of five were able to pick out the stranded men because of the lifeboat men’s survival gear that shone like beacons.","Capt Hills said: “We couldn’t actually touch down because of the contour of the land and the bushes, but we held steady long enough to get everyone on board.","{{28}}"],"bank":[{"key":"A","text":"Michael Vlasto, the operations director of the RNLI, said: “We are very grateful to the Royal Navy for airlifting our two volunteer crewmen back on board the lifeboat, and getting the two yachtsmen safely to dry land.”"},{"key":"B","text":"When the lifeboat reached the scene, the captain realised he could not get his lifeboat close enough to the scene and launched the lifeboat’s inflatable vessel which filled with water and trapped the two lifeboat men along with the yachtsman on the reef. However, the Royal Navy Sea King helicopter was en route to the scene."},{"key":"C","text":"The two-man lifeboat crew became trapped on a sliver of reef along with a stranded yachtsman they had been attempting to rescue."},{"key":"D","text":"The hospital spokesman said: “They were feeling fine and have been discharged.”"},{"key":"E","text":"Once on land, he used his mobile phone to summon the rescue services."},{"key":"F","text":"It was a good operation; we got the other guy, too. Thankfully, all is well that ends well.”"},{"key":"G","text":"The pilot, Captain Ian Hills, then gingerly moved his Sea King helicopter toward a tiny island off the coast of Jura, in the Inner Hebrides, where he was able to pick up a second stranded yachtsman."}],"items":[{"n":0,"example":true,"answer":"C"},{"n":24,"answer":"G"},{"n":25,"answer":"A"},{"n":26,"answer":"E"},{"n":27,"answer":"B"},{"n":28,"answer":"F"}]}$mtr$::jsonb) on conflict (task_id) do update set task = excluded.task;
insert into public.tasks (id, exam_id, section, number, kind, exam_type, points, position, content, audio) values ($mtr$2007-okt-emelt-L1$mtr$, $mtr$2007-okt-emelt$mtr$, $mtr$language$mtr$, 1, $mtr$choice$mtr$, $mtr$feleletválasztós szövegkiegészítés (A-D)$mtr$, 10, 5, $mtr${"id":"2007-okt-emelt-L1","number":1,"kind":"choice","layout":"inline","examType":"feleletválasztós szövegkiegészítés (A-D)","points":10,"instructions":["You are going to read an article about hamburgers. Some words are missing from the text.","Choose the most appropriate answer from the options (A-D) for each gap (1-10) in the text."],"title":"BURGER SERVED WITH LEGAL WARNING","body":["Diners wanting to taste a restaurant's £12 gourmet burgers last week {{0}} they had to sign a disclaimer. The document stated that the restaurant was not responsible for the consequences.","Managers at the Marriott West India Quay in east London's Docklands asked customers to complete the form {{1}} rare or medium-rare meat. The chef on duty also had to sign the paper, {{2}} said the restaurant should not be held responsible for food-poisoning. Customers {{3}} have their burgers cooked \"medium or above\" instead to reduce the risk.","A spokesman for Marriott said they stopped {{4}} the forms on Monday but warned customers they had the rare or medium-rare burgers \"at their own risk\". She added: \"We should {{5}} that we have full confidence in the meat products that we serve. {{6}}, customers who choose to have their burgers cooked rare or medium rare {{7}} at their own risk.\"","Nick Scade, chairman of the Restaurant Association, said: \"I {{8}} heard of anything like this before - and it's not something {{9}} in my restaurant. You've got to have a bit of common sense somewhere in life and if a customer wants to order raw meat they have to {{10}} responsibility for the risk they are taking.\""],"items":[{"n":0,"options":[{"key":"A","text":"refused"},{"key":"B","text":"will accept"},{"key":"C","text":"were told"},{"key":"D","text":"were asked"}],"example":true,"answer":"C"},{"n":1,"options":[{"key":"A","text":"unless they wanted"},{"key":"B","text":"if they asked"},{"key":"C","text":"so they ordered"},{"key":"D","text":"if they wanted"}]},{"n":2,"options":[{"key":"A","text":"which"},{"key":"B","text":"what"},{"key":"C","text":"Ø"},{"key":"D","text":"who"}]},{"n":3,"options":[{"key":"A","text":"allowed the chef"},{"key":"B","text":"happened to"},{"key":"C","text":"were urged to"},{"key":"D","text":"were used to"}]},{"n":4,"options":[{"key":"A","text":"to use"},{"key":"B","text":"having used"},{"key":"C","text":"using"},{"key":"D","text":"being used"}]},{"n":5,"options":[{"key":"A","text":"realise"},{"key":"B","text":"call attention"},{"key":"C","text":"care about"},{"key":"D","text":"point out"}]},{"n":6,"options":[{"key":"A","text":"Moreover"},{"key":"B","text":"Although"},{"key":"C","text":"However"},{"key":"D","text":"Otherwise"}]},{"n":7,"options":[{"key":"A","text":"do so"},{"key":"B","text":"eat that"},{"key":"C","text":"will do"},{"key":"D","text":"order it"}]},{"n":8,"options":[{"key":"A","text":"could have"},{"key":"B","text":"certainly haven’t"},{"key":"C","text":"probably haven’t"},{"key":"D","text":"might have"}]},{"n":9,"options":[{"key":"A","text":"I have been done"},{"key":"B","text":"I’ll include"},{"key":"C","text":"I’ll be doing"},{"key":"D","text":"I encourage it"}]},{"n":10,"options":[{"key":"A","text":"take any"},{"key":"B","text":"accept altogether"},{"key":"C","text":"take up"},{"key":"D","text":"accept some"}]}]}$mtr$::jsonb, null)
