ell as their breathing, heartbeat, and muscle activity.","gapCount":2},{"n":18,"stem":"It’s been confirmed that all {{gap}} and {{gap}} studied with the EEG do actually sleep.","gapCount":2},{"n":19,"stem":"At the same time, however, there is some {{gap}} that {{gap}}, such as snakes and turtles do not truly sleep.","gapCount":2},{"n":20,"stem":"Good sleepers are nearly all {{gap}}, while poor sleepers are animals that are prey for predators, so they must be watching out for {{gap}}.","gapCount":2}],"grading":{"spelling":"lenient"}}$mtr$::jsonb, $mtr${"file":"e_angol_13maj_fl.mp3","start":604.57,"end":1211.05,"clip":"hang/e_angol_13maj_fl_H2.mp3"}$mtr$::jsonb)
