ol.","But Keith dreamed of owning a freehold farm in Botswana and returning it to its original beauty, so the family moved on from Selebi after five years to a 2,000-acre farm in south- eastern Botswana. This was an intensely green, watery wonderland, with crocodiles, hippos and antelope, and teamed with bird life.","Molope Farm was thrilling − a “ferocious but fragile” paradise. Tighter schedules, tests and homework came as the children moved on to secondary schools across the borders in Zimbabwe and South Africa. And as the children became increasingly independent, their parents were ever more caught up with their own campaigns − Keith with Aids awareness and alternative therapies; Linda with her nutritional studies and books.","Twenty Chickens for a Saddle is such a bravura performance that it is difficult to believe it is Robyn Scott’s first book. It is a confident portrait of a rollicking family that championed laughter and independence of thought and action at every turn.","(telegraph.co.uk)"],"items":[{"n":0,"example":true,"stem":"The book Twenty Chickens for a Saddle describes","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Robyn Scott’s first seven years."},{"key":"B","text":"the parents’ nostalgia for New Zealand."},{"key":"C","text":"the life of Robyn’s family in Africa."},{"key":"D","text":"the hardships the family faced in Africa."}],"answer":"C"},{"n":25,"stem":"The family’s first home in Africa was","options":[{"key":"A","text":"only fit for cows."},{"key":"B","text":"less than luxurious."},{"key":"C","text":"too small for the family."},{"key":"D","text":"too terrifying for the children."}],"answer":"B"},{"n":26,"stem":"Keith, who was a doctor,","options":[{"key":"A","text":"suffered from a chronic eye infection."},{"key":"B","text":"went on long expeditions with his children."},{"key":"C","text":"was often too tired to talk to his family."},{"key":"D","text":"shared his experiences with his family."}],"answer":"D"},{"n":27,"stem":"In Selebi the children’s life was","options":[{"key":"A","text":"exhausting."},{"key":"B","text":"monotonous."},{"key":"C","text":"unstructured."},{"key":"D","text":"unconventional."}],"answer":"D"},{"n":28,"stem":"Young Robyn","options":[{"key":"A","text":"was given a new saddle for her pony."},{"key":"B","text":"kept various animals in the back-yard."},{"key":"C","text":"was concerned about animal welfare."},{"key":"D","text":"was especially fond of reptiles."}],"answer":"C"},{"n":29,"stem":"The family moved to Malope Farm in order to","options":[{"key":"A","text":"fulfill Keith’s dreams."},{"key":"B","text":"live a truly African life."},{"key":"C","text":"own a larger piece of land."},{"key":"D","text":"be closer to the children’s schools."}],"answer":"A"},{"n":30,"stem":"As the children became older,","options":[{"key":"A","text":"they gradually lost interest in Malope Farm."},{"key":"B","text":"the parents became more and more attached to the farm."},{"key":"C","text":"the different members of the family lived their own lives and pursued their own interests."},{"key":"D","text":"Linda spent most of her time studying plants and writing books on nutrition."}],"answer":"C"}]}$mtr$::jsonb) on conflict (task_id) do update set task = excluded.task;
