et somewhere in the world."}],"answer":["A"]},{"n":5,"stem":"Morgaine Gaye says that insects will probably be …","options":[{"key":"A","text":"roasted and served on a plate."},{"key":"B","text":"used as ingredients in burgers and sausages."}],"answer":["B"]},{"n":6,"stem":"According to Morgaine Gaye …","options":[{"key":"A","text":"every third person in the world regularly eats insects."},{"key":"B","text":"wasps are a Japanese speciality."}],"answer":["A","B"]},{"n":7,"stem":"Morgaine Gaye says that insects will become a popular part of Western diet if …","options":[{"key":"A","text":"people cannot see that they are eating insects."},{"key":"B","text":"they are given a new name."}],"answer":["B"]}]}$mtr$::jsonb) on conflict (task_id) do update set task = excluded.task;
insert into public.tasks (id, exam_id, section, number, kind, exam_type, points, position, content, audio) values ($mtr$2015-maj-emelt-H2$mtr$, $mtr$2015-maj-emelt$mtr$, $mtr$listening$mtr$, 2, $mtr$choice$mtr$, $mtr$igaz / hamis / a szöveg nem mondja (A/B/C)$mtr$, 13, 10, $mtr${"id":"2015-maj-emelt-H2","number":2,"kind":"choice","layout":"stems","examType":"igaz / hamis / a szöveg nem mondja (A/B/C)","points":13,"instructions":["In this section you will hear an interview with Sarah Morgan, an American businesswoman who runs a speed dating service in London.","Your task will be to decide whether the following statements are true, false or we do not know because the text does not say, and write the appropriate letter in the boxes on the right. Write A if the statement is true, write B if the statement is false, and write C if the text does not say.","First, you will have some time to look at the task, and then we will play the whole recording in one piece.","Then, you will hear the recording again, but this time we will play the text in shorter sections to give you enough time to write down your answers."],"audio":{"file":"e_angol_15maj_fl.mp3","start":510.04,"end":1192.42,"clip":"hang/e_angol_15maj_fl_H2.mp3"},"items":[{"n":0,"example":true,"stem":"Sarah is the manager of a dating agency in the capital of the UK.","answer":"A"},{"n":8,"stem":"Sarah defines speed dating as a system whose main aim is to help people meet a lot of new people."},{"n":9,"stem":"The length of the chats varies depending on the number of participants in the event."},{"n":10,"stem":"After the signal the men have a minute to move on to the next date."},{"n":11,"stem":"If one person likes another person, their email address will be automatically forwarded to the other party."},{"n":12,"stem":"Sarah is the first businessperson to have introduced speed dating to the British market."},{"n":13,"stem":"Such events are sometimes organised for specific groups of people."},{"n":14,"stem":"Speed dating events are better for meeting new people than ordinary bars or discos, because it is obvious why everybody is there."},{"n":15,"stem":"You have to prove that you are single to be allowed to attend a speed dating event."},{"n":16,"stem":"People don’t know whether they’ve been chosen by a particular person until two days after the event."},{"n":17,"stem":"Most people agree that the time limit is enough to decide if a person is a hopeless case."},{"n":18,"stem":"According to the Edinburgh study, the majority of people arrive at a decision in less than 30 seconds."},{"n":19,"stem":"The most important thing about a woman for most men is her face."},{"n":20,"stem":"The most important thing about a man for most women is his height."}],"options":[{"key":"A","text":"TRUE"},{"key":"B","text":"FALSE"},{"key":"C","text":"THE TEXT DOES NOT SAY"}]}$mtr$::jsonb, $mtr${"file":"e_angol_15maj_fl.mp3","start":510.04,"end":1192.42,"clip":"hang/e_angol_15maj_fl_H2.mp3"}$mtr$::jsonb)
