g. Murder on Smith Street ̶ it is treating your potential audience with contempt to then have a picture of a dead body next to a sign saying 'Smith Street'.","Don't try to tell the whole story One common cover design error is particularly difficult for authors to overcome: they know their own books too well. As a result of this, many try to include as much as they can on the cover. This does not sell books. Firstly, the reader is overwhelmed by the confusion and secondly, what may seem like a really important part of your story to you, may mean nothing to a reader before they have read the book. Choose one or two salient points from your story to include and keep it simple. You need to create an emotion in the reader that makes them want to read the book, not tell them what the book is all about.","Show your genre/tone What images come to mind when you think 'thriller'? Obviously, a pretty vase of flowers is not going to grab you if you're a thriller fan. Break the vase and maybe have a bullet lying in amongst the bent flowers, with blood in place of spilled water, and you have a different cover altogether. It's about giving the reader an idea.","(Writing Magazine)"],"items":[{"n":0,"example":true,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"With electronically printed books the cover is of little interest."},{"key":"B","text":"The reader's reaction to a book cover is of great importance."},{"key":"C","text":"The cover for an ebook should look different from a print copy."},{"key":"D","text":"Ebooks and print copies need similar covers to impress the reader."}],"answer":"B"},{"n":26,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Writers are often uncertain about how to design a book cover."},{"key":"B","text":"Even professionals sometimes make mistakes designing covers."},{"key":"C","text":"Sales are more influenced by the quality of the writing than the cover."},{"key":"D","text":"Even if finances are tight, one shouldn't economise on the cover of a book."}],"answer":"A"},{"n":27,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"There aren't any rules to observe in designing book covers."},{"key":"B","text":"Some book covers do not serve their original purpose at all."},{"key":"C","text":"Ebook and print book covers should look completely different."},{"key":"D","text":"The essential point about the cover is the same for ebooks and print books."}],"answer":"D"},{"n":28,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Non-professional covers don't give enough protection to print books."},{"key":"B","text":"Chip Kidd (of Jurassic Park) thinks the cover should make the content clear."},{"key":"C","text":"Catching the eye of the potential reader is the main purpose of a book cover."},{"key":"D","text":"Covers are best if they follow the title of the book as closely as possible."}],"answer":"C"},{"n":29,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Writers are often the best designers of the cover as they know their books best."},{"key":"B","text":"Writers usually know what things from the book interest readers most."},{"key":"C","text":"Covers work best if they just emphasize a couple of important points."},{"key":"D","text":"The more details about the story are given on the cover the better."}],"answer":"C"},{"n":30,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"A crime story does not need to show blood on the front cover."},{"key":"B","text":"The cover should be in harmony with the genre of the book."},{"key":"C","text":"Flowers are out of place if you want thriller fans to notice a book."},{"key":"D","text":"Spilled water can occasionally be as dramatic as spilled blood."}],"answer":"B"}]}$mtr$::jsonb) on conflict (task_id) do update set task = excluded.task;
insert into public.tasks (id, exam_id, section, number, kind, exam_type, points, position, content, audio) values ($mtr$2015-okt-emelt-L1$mtr$, $mtr$2015-okt-emelt$mtr$, $mtr$language$mtr$, 1, $mtr$text$mtr$, $mtr$szóképzés (zárójeles szó)$mtr$, 9, 5, $mtr${"id":"2015-okt-emelt-L1","number":1,"kind":"text","layout":"inline","examType":"szóképzés (zárójeles szó)","points":9,"instructions":["You are going to read an article about the oldest wine cellar in the world. Some words are missing from the text.","Use the words in brackets to form the words that fit in the gaps (1-9).","There might be cases when you do not have to change the word in brackets.","Use only one word for each gap."],"title":"OLDEST WINE CELLAR FOUND IN ANCIENT SITE","body":["A 3,700-year-old wine cellar has been unearthed in the {{0}} of a Canaanite palace in Israel, potentially {{1}} modern man a true taste of the past.","Samples from the ceramic jars suggest they held a {{2}} beverage that was evidently reserved for banquets, researchers said.","Andrew Koh of Brandeis University found {{3}} of ingredients that may have included honey, mint, cedar, tree resins and cinnamon. Chemical {{4}} indicates that the jars held red wine and possibly white wine, Koh said. No liquid was left, and he analyzed residues he had {{5}} from the jars.","{{6}} found 40 ceramic jars, each big enough to hold about 13 gallons, in a single room. There may be more wine {{7}} yet to be found. A few days before the dig ended, the team discovered two doors leading out of the wine cellar, which may point toward {{8}} storage rooms. Patrick McGovern of the University of Pennsylvania, an expert in ancient winemaking, said the {{9}} “sheds important new light” on the development of winemaking in ancient Canaan, from where it later spread to Egypt and across the Mediterranean.","(http://www.bloomberg.com)"],"grading":{"spelling":"strict"},"items":[{"n":0,"prompt":"ruin","example":true,"accept":["ruins"]},{"n":1,"prompt":"offer"},{"n":2,"prompt":"luxury"},{"n":3,"prompt":"sign"},{"n":4,"prompt":"analyze"},{"n":5,"prompt":"move"},{"n":6,"prompt":"archaeology"},{"n":7,"prompt":"contain"},{"n":8,"prompt":"add"},{"n":9,"prompt":"discover"}]}$mtr$::jsonb, null)
