ed from sleeping on a train that has reached the end of the line. Those who refuse to comply could be kicked off by authorities, the regulation says. A separate measure that would have barred people who let off noxious odors was removed from the rules, Masui said. Supporters of disadvantaged Sacramentans said that this particular rule would have been a blow for homeless people, who have a right to ride buses and trains.","The rules will be implemented once officials finalize remaining details and customers are notified of the changes.","(ibtimes.co.uk)"],"bank":[{"key":"A","text":"to get around by car than by public transit."},{"key":"B","text":"to find their way around."},{"key":"C","text":"to get off according to new regulations."},{"key":"D","text":"to stay asleep on a vehicle after it gets to the terminal."},{"key":"E","text":"to attract many people to the city center."},{"key":"F","text":"to drink alcohol before getting on a bus."},{"key":"G","text":"to switch to using public transit."},{"key":"H","text":"to convince more people to use them."},{"key":"I","text":"to prevent homeless people from using trains and buses."},{"key":"K","text":"to be allowed on a bus."},{"key":"L","text":"to pay extra for the cleaning."}],"items":[{"n":0,"example":true,"stem":"If you sleep on a bus in Sacramento, you will be asked","answer":"C"},{"n":24,"stem":"Significant real-estate development is expected","answer":"E"},{"n":25,"stem":"Improving public transit services is expected","answer":"H"},{"n":26,"stem":"The layout of the city makes it easier for people","answer":"A"},{"n":27,"stem":"Due to, for example, the high crime rate, middle class people are reluctant","answer":"G"},{"n":28,"stem":"According to the new regulations, you will need to be fully clothed","answer":"K"},{"n":29,"stem":"In future you will be in trouble if you happen","answer":"D"},{"n":30,"stem":"A possibly unintended result of another rule would have been","answer":"I"}]}$mtr$::jsonb) on conflict (task_id) d