er (or duster).","\"Women are still working what Arkie Hochschild called \"The second shift\" back in 1989,\" explains occupational psychologist Almuth McDonall. \"I expected the gender difference to be smaller in couples where both partners worked full-time, but it was even bigger. I think this is because the working mothers felt guilty, so they had to do even more.\"","So who is this mysterious man? In his bio he claims to be a \"frazzled working dad with a wife and three kids who spends his 'me time' on Twitter.\" When asked for an interview for this newspaper, he said he was \"too busy juggling savoury yoghurts, kids' sportswear, healthy- looking skin, a career & pasta salads\" to answer my questions.","The Man Who Has It All says: \"If I can help one man stay hydrated, I'll be a happy man\", but maybe it's more than a joke. If the popularity of this account encourages one father to step up his share of childcare, or challenges one woman to realise she might not be \"very lucky\" to have a man who \"helps with the kids on weekends\", then we might all be \"#Blessed\".","(The Independent)"],"bank":[{"key":"A","text":"women's magazines."},{"key":"B","text":"least equal."},{"key":"C","text":"a Man Who Has It All."},{"key":"D","text":"childcare."},{"key":"E","text":"old clichés."},{"key":"F","text":"gender equality issues."},{"key":"G","text":"supportive statements."},{"key":"H","text":"in character."},{"key":"I","text":"on weekends."},{"key":"K","text":"the situation."},{"key":"L","text":"in the house."},{"key":"M","text":"sexist."}],"items":[{"n":0,"example":true,"stem":"The author of the parody Twitter account calls himself","answer":"C"},{"n":1,"stem":"The microblogs treat, in a light-hearted way,","answer":"F"},{"n":2,"stem":"In his blog The Man deliberately uses","answer":"E"},{"n":3,"stem":"The account ridicules staple advice found in","answer":"A"},{"n":4,"stem":"People may not even realize their remarks are","answer":"M"},{"n":5,"stem":"The fact that many women work full time hasn't changed","answer":"K"},{"n":6,"stem":"Women married to middle- class men have been found","answer":"B"},{"n":7,"stem":"Working mothers often compensate by doing more","answer":"L"},{"n":8,"stem":"When asked for an interview, The Man answered","answer":"H"}]}$mtr$::jsonb) on conflict (task_id) do update set task = excluded.task;
insert into public.tasks (id, exam_id, section, number, kind, exam_type, points, position, content, audio) values ($mtr$2018-okt-emelt-R2$mtr$, $mtr$2018-okt-emelt$mtr$, $mtr$reading$mtr$, 2, $mtr$bank$mtr$, $mtr$mondatrész visszahelyezése szövegbe$mtr$, 8, 2, $mtr${"id":"2018-okt-emelt-R2","number":2,"kind":"bank","layout":"inline","examType":"mondatrész visszahelyezése szövegbe","points":8,"instructions":["In this article about English Renaissance dramatists some parts of sentences have been left out.","Your task is to reconstruct the text by filling in the gaps from the list.","There are two extra letters that you will not need."],"title":"CHRISTOPHER MARLOWE CREDITED AS ONE OF SHAKESPEARE'S CO-WRITERS","body":["The long-held suggestion that Christopher Marlowe was William Shakespeare is now widely dismissed, {{0}}. But Marlowe is enjoying the next best thing – {{9}}with a credit as co-writer of the three Henry VI plays. The two dramatists will appear jointly on each of the three title pages of the plays within the New Oxford Shakespeare, {{10}}.","Using old-fashioned scholarship and 21st-century computerised tools to analyse texts, the edition’s international scholars have contended that {{11}} was far more extensive than has been realised until now. Lead researcher Gary Taylor told the Guardian: “The orthodox view was that Shakespeare didn’t collaborate at all. What has happened in the past two or three decades is that {{12}} that we underestimated the amount of Shakespeare’s work that’s collaborative.”","Taylor said these editions of the Henry VI plays are the first {{13}}. “We have been able to verify his presence in those three plays strongly and clearly enough,” he added. The findings shed new light on the supposed rivalry between Marlowe and Shakespeare. Taylor added: “We can now be confident that {{14}}. Rivals sometimes collaborate.”","Decisions about authorship have been supported by {{15}}. The researchers believe that computerised textual analysis is now so sophisticated that they can even distinguish between Shakespeare writing under Marlowe’s influence and Marlowe writing alone. Taylor acknowledges that {{16}}: “You can’t say anything about Shakespeare without somebody disagreeing with you, but our knowledge of the past increases by debate of this kind.”","(guardian.co.uk)"],"bank":[{"key":"A","text":"the accumulation of new scholarship, techniques and resources has made it clear"},{"key":"B","text":"a complex jigsaw of different kinds of evidence"},{"key":"C","text":"along with other authorship theories"},{"key":"D","text":"Shakespeare’s collaboration with other playwrights"},{"key":"E","text":"doubts may still be cast on their conclusions"},{"key":"F","text":"taking centre stage alongside his great Elizabethan rival"},{"key":"G","text":"they didn’t just influence each other"},{"key":"H","text":"they never worked with each other"},{"key":"I","text":"a landmark project to be published this month"},{"key":"K","text":"to bring the author’s identity into question"},{"key":"L","text":"to identify Marlowe’s contribution"}],"items":[{"n":0,"example":true,"answer":"C"},{"n":9},{"n":10},{"n":11},{"n":12},{"n":13},{"n":14},{"n":15},{"n":16}]}$mtr$::jsonb, null)
insert into public.task_keys (task_id, task) values ($mtr$2018-okt-emelt-R2$mtr$, $mtr${"id":"2018-okt-emelt-R2","number":2,"kind":"bank","layout":"inline","examType":"mondatrész visszahelyezése szövegbe","points":8,"instructions":["In this article about English Renaissance dramatists some parts of sentences have been left out.","Your task is to reconstruct the text by filling in the gaps from the list.","There are two extra letters that you will not need."],"title":"CHRISTOPHER MARLOWE CREDITED AS ONE OF SHAKESPEARE'S CO-WRITERS","body":["The long-held suggestion that Christopher Marlowe was William Shakespeare is now widely dismissed, {{0}}. But Marlowe is enjoying the next best thing – {{9}}with a credit as co-writer of the three Henry VI plays. The two dramatists will appear jointly on each of the three title pages of the plays within the New Oxford Shakespeare, {{10}}.","Using old-fashioned scholarship and 21st-century computerised tools to analyse texts, the edition’s international scholars have contended that {{11}} was far more extensive than has been realised until now. Lead researcher Gary Taylor told the Guardian: “The orthodox view was that Shakespeare didn’t collaborate at all. What has happened in the past two or three decades is that {{12}} that we underestimated the amount of Shakespeare’s work that’s collaborative.”","Taylor said these editions of the Henry VI plays are the first {{13}}. “We have been able to verify his presence in those three plays strongly and clearly enough,” he added. The findings shed new light on the supposed rivalry between Marlowe and Shakespeare. Taylor added: “We can now be confident that {{14}}. Rivals sometimes collaborate.”","Decisions about authorship have been supported by {{15}}. The researchers believe that computerised textual analysis is now so sophisticated that they can even distinguish between Shakespeare writing under Marlowe’s influence and Marlowe writing alone. Taylor acknowledges that {{16}}: “You can’t say anything about Shakespeare without somebody disagreeing with you, but our knowledge of the past increases by debate of this kind.”","(guardian.co.uk)"],"bank":[{"key":"A","text":"the accumulation of new scholarship, techniques and resources has made it clear"},{"key":"B","text":"a complex jigsaw of different kinds of evidence"},{"key":"C","text":"along with other authorship theories"},{"key":"D","text":"Shakespeare’s collaboration with other playwrights"},{"key":"E","text":"doubts may still be cast on their conclusions"},{"key":"F","text":"taking centre stage alongside his great Elizabethan rival"},{"key":"G","text":"they didn’t just influence each other"},{"key":"H","text":"they never worked with each other"},{"key":"I","text":"a landmark project to be published this month"},{"key":"K","text":"to bring the author’s identity into question"},{"key":"L","text":"to identify Marlowe’s contribution"}],"items":[{"n":0,"example":true,"answer":"C"},{"n":9,"answer":"F"},{"n":10,"answer":"I"},{"n":11,"answer":"D"},{"n":12,"answer":"A"},{"n":13,"answer":"L"},{"n":14,"answer":"G"},{"n":15,"answer":"B"},{"n":16,"answer":"E"}]}$mtr$::jsonb) on conflict (task_id) do update set task = excluded.task;
insert into public.tasks (id, exam_id, section, number, kind, exam_type, points, position, content, audio) values ($mtr$2018-okt-emelt-R3$mtr$, $mtr$2018-okt-emelt$mtr$, $mtr$reading$mtr$, 3, $mtr$choice$mtr$, $mtr$feleletválasztás a szöveg alapján (A-D)$mtr$, 5, 3, $mtr${"id":"2018-okt-emelt-R3","number":3,"kind":"choice","layout":"stems","examType":"feleletválasztás a szöveg alapján (A-D)","points":5,"instructions":["Read through this article about a new craze and then read the multiple-choice questions (17-21) following it.","Your task is to choose the alternative (A-D) that best corresponds to what the text says."],"title":"TODAY'S HIPSTERS ARE FLOCKING TO MEDIEVAL MEAD LIKE BEES TO HONEY","body":["There have been many baffling food trends over the past couple of years, but none is quite so odd as the comeback of mead. I say comeback, but that suggests mead had slipped off the radar for a couple of years. In fact, the last time the drink was truly fashionable was in the 9th century.","Mead, made using fermented honey, is probably the oldest known alcoholic drink, whose origins stretch back 9,000 years. It is referenced in Chaucer and frequently in the old English epic poem Beowulf, where Viking warriors tended to go looting and burning villages after getting drunk in the mead hall.","But after a good 600 years of falling off drinks menus in taverns in favour of beer and wine, mead is back with a zing. According to the American Mead Makers Association, sales went up 42 per cent last year. In the UK, Cornish Mead said sales had gone up 15 per cent in recent weeks alone.","Various people have suggested that Game of Thrones, the cultish television programme set in the futuristic and yet medieval kingdoms of Westeros and Eosos, is responsible. The characters certainly drown goblets of intoxicating liquor, but mead is never actually mentioned in the programme or in the original Game of Thrones books.","The cause of mead's sudden popularity are hipsters, those bearded young urbanites who, having helped launch cereal-only cafés, have found mead as the next novelty drink after craft beer. In the endless quest for the new, mead is a perfect candidate with its unique flavour of fermented honey.","Mead's cause has also been helped by a general move towards \"authenticity\" in food and drink. People are far more interested in traditional methods of food production, which also explains the rise of sourdough bread and the whole slow food movement. At various real ale festivals there are now dedicated mead bars, displaying a wide range of this low-alcohol drink from the sickly sweet to the semi-dry.","(The Daily Telegraph)"],"items":[{"n":0,"example":true,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Mead's new popularity is a puzzling phenomenon."},{"key":"B","text":"Young people drink too much mead."},{"key":"C","text":"Mead goes well with trendy new foods."},{"key":"D","text":"Mead is a social drink to be enjoyed in company."}],"answer":"A"},{"n":17,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"The Vikings spread the custom of mead-drinking."},{"key":"B","text":"It is easy to get drunk on mead."},{"key":"C","text":"Honey is an indispensable ingredient of mead."},{"key":"D","text":"Mead has been in and out of fashion for over a thousand years."}]},{"n":18,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Mead sales have gone up in the US more than in Britain."},{"key":"B","text":"Mead's popularity is growing on both sides of the Atlantic."},{"key":"C","text":"Mead is unknown outside Britain or the US."},{"key":"D","text":"British sales are now catching up with American sales."}]},{"n":19,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"The cult series Games of Thrones has added to the popularity of mead."},{"key":"B","text":"In Westeros and Eosos mead is drunk in large quantities."},{"key":"C","text":"In the two kingdoms the characters often get drunk."},{"key":"D","text":"The series' influence on mead's new popularity is far from obvious."}]},{"n":20,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Mead is now a more popular drink than craft beer."},{"key":"B","text":"Cereal-only cafés are mostly run by hipsters."},{"key":"C","text":"Hipsters came to like craft beer and mead in this order."},{"key":"D","text":"Mead is mainly to be had in cereal-only cafés."}]},{"n":21,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Sourdough bread and mead are popular for the same reason."},{"key":"B","text":"Real ale festivals have been promoted by the slow food movement."},{"key":"C","text":"Making sourdough bread is a slow process."},{"key":"D","text":"Sourdough bread is served at traditional real ale festivals."}]}]}$mtr$::jsonb, null)
