text":"DeFauw is thankful she had the opportunity to get to go back to school and get her degree. “It’s nice to finish something you started,” she said."},{"key":"C","text":"Joyce DeFauw started her freshman year at Northern Illinois University in 1951 with a plan to graduate with a degree in home economics."},{"key":"D","text":"Flash forward to 2019, when DeFauw showed interest in the college education she left behind."},{"key":"E","text":"“At times I wanted to quit, because I was really lonely. But I didn’t.” DeFauw said. She said she had plenty of encouragement from family, friends and the school."},{"key":"F","text":"The special man was Don Freeman. The two got married in 1955, and had three children together before Freeman passed away, leaving her widowed for about five years."},{"key":"G","text":"“When we made calls to the school, they were shocked to hear we were asking about a student from the 50s,” one of her granddaughters said."},{"key":"H","text":"She planned to write her thesis about getting a degree in old age. “Believe it or not, I’m not the only one,” she says, laughing."},{"key":"I","text":"“It was my first computer,” DeFauw said. “My children had to teach me how to use it.”"}],"items":[{"n":0,"example":true,"answer":"C"},{"n":22,"answer":"F"},{"n":23,"answer":"D"},{"n":24,"answer":"G"},{"n":25,"answer":"I"},{"n":26,"answer":"E"},{"n":27,"answer":"B"}],"source":"https://edition.cnn.com/2022/12/11/us/90-year-old-woman-graduates-college-"}$mtr$::jsonb) on conflict (task_id) do update set task = excluded.task;
insert into public.tasks (id, exam_id, section, number, kind, exam_type, points, position, content, audio) values ($mtr$2023-maj-emelt-L1$mtr$, $mtr$2023-maj-emelt$mtr$, $mtr$language$mtr$, 1, $mtr$text$mtr$, $mtr$szóképzés (zárójeles szó)$mtr$, 9, 5, $mtr${"id":"2023-maj-emelt-L1","number":1,"kind":"text","layout":"inline","examType":"szóképzés (zárójeles szó)","points":9,"instructions":["You are going to read an article about a new business.","Some words are missing from the text.","Use the words in brackets to form the words that fit in the gaps (1-9).","There might be cases when you do not have to change the word in brackets.","Use only one word for each gap."],"title":"BOSTON SNOW BUSINESS","body":["What is crazier than a guy in snowbound Massachusetts boxing up the {{0}} white stuff and offering it for {{1}} online?","A man in {{2}} Boston is selling snow online to customers in warmer states. For $89, {{3}} entrepreneur Kyle Waring will ship you 6 pounds of Boston- area snow in an insulated Styrofoam box – enough for 10 to 15 snowballs, he says. And people are actually buying it. His social media {{4}} claim to have filled more than 133 orders for snow – more than 30 on Tuesday alone, his busiest day yet.","With more than 45 total inches, Boston has set a record this winter for the {{5}} month in its history. Most {{6}} see the huge piles of snow as a nuisance, but Waring saw an opportunity.","It all started a few weeks ago, when Waring and his wife were shoveling deep snow from their yard in Manchester-by-the-Sea, a {{7}} suburb north of Boston. He joked about {{8}} the stuff to friends and family in warmer states, and an idea was born.","Whether Waring can sustain his popular venture into the spring remains to be seen. But he has no {{9}} of product. “At this rate, it’s going to be July before the snow melts,” he told Boston.com."],"grading":{"spelling":"strict"},"items":[{"n":0,"prompt":"powder","example":true,"accept":["powdery"]},{"n":1,"prompt":"sell"},{"n":2,"prompt":"suburb"},{"n":3,"prompt":"invent"},{"n":4,"prompt":"count"},{"n":5,"prompt":"snow"},{"n":6,"prompt":"reside"},{"n":7,"prompt":"coast"},{"n":8,"prompt":"ship"},{"n":9,"prompt":"short"}]}$mtr$::jsonb, null)
insert into public.task_keys (task_id, task) values ($mtr$2023-maj-emelt-L1$mtr$, $mtr${"id":"2023-maj-emelt-L1","number":1,"kind":"text","layout":"inline","examType":"szóképzés (zárójeles szó)","points":9,"instructions":["You are going to read an article about a new business.","Some words are missing from the text.","Use the words in brackets to form the words that fit in the gaps (1-9).","There might be cases when you do not have to change the word in brackets.","Use only one word for each gap."],"title":"BOSTON SNOW BUSINESS","body":["What is crazier than a guy in snowbound Massachusetts boxing up the {{0}} white stuff and offering it for {{1}} online?","A man in {{2}} Boston is selling snow online to customers in warmer states. For $89, {{3}} entrepreneur Kyle Waring will ship you 6 pounds of Boston- area snow in an insulated Styrofoam box – enough for 10 to 15 snowballs, he says. And people are actually buying it. His social media {{4}} claim to have filled more than 133 orders for snow – more than 30 on Tuesday alone, his busiest day yet.","With more than 45 total inches, Boston has set a record this winter for the {{5}} month in its history. Most {{6}} see the huge piles of snow as a nuisance, but Waring saw an opportunity.","It all started a few weeks ago, when Waring and his wife were shoveling deep snow from their yard in Manchester-by-the-Sea, a {{7}} suburb north of Boston. He joked about {{8}} the stuff to friends and family in warmer states, and an idea was born.","Whether Waring can sustain his popular venture into the spring remains to be seen. But he has no {{9}} of product. “At this rate, it’s going to be July before the snow melts,” he told Boston.com."],"grading":{"spelling":"strict","maxWords":1},"items":[{"n":0,"prompt":"powder","example":true,"accept":["powdery"]},{"n":1,"prompt":"sell","accept":["sale"]},{"n":2,"prompt":"suburb","accept":["suburban","suburbian"]},{"n":3,"prompt":"invent","accept":["inventive","inventor","inventious"]},{"n":4,"prompt":"count","accept":["accounts"]},{"n":5,"prompt":"snow","accept":["snowiest"]},{"n":6,"prompt":"reside","accept":["residents"]},{"n":7,"prompt":"coast","accept":["coastal"]},{"n":8,"prompt":"ship","accept":["shipping"]},{"n":9,"prompt":"short","accept":["shortage","shortfall"]}]}$mtr$::jsonb) on conflict (task_id) do update set task = excluded.task;
insert into public.tasks (id, exam_id, section, number, kind, exam_type, points, position, content, audio) values ($mtr$2023-maj-emelt-L2$mtr$, $mtr$2023-maj-emelt$mtr$, $mtr$language$mtr$, 2, $mtr$choice$mtr$, $mtr$feleletválasztós szövegkiegészítés (A-D)$mtr$, 8, 6, $mtr${"id":"2023-maj-emelt-L2","number":2,"kind":"choice","layout":"inline","examType":"feleletválasztós szövegkiegészítés (A-D)","points":8,"instructions":["You are going to read an article about the success of the French baguette. Some words are missing from the text.","Choose the most appropriate answer from the options (A-D) for each gap (10-17) in the text."],"title":"FRENCH BAGUETTE GETS UNESCO HERITAGE STATUS","body":["There are few things {{0}} uniquely French than the humble baguette. {{10}}, the baguette has been in decline in recent years, as traditional bakeries struggle against the rise of large supermarkets and the increasing popularity of sourdough.","But now {{11}} to celebrate, as UNESCO adds the baguette to its cultural heritage list. The body announced that it {{12}} \"the special know-how and culture of baguette bread\" to its list of 600 other items, joining things like traditional tea making in China and a Korean mask dance – both also included for the first time in 2022.","Its inclusion \"celebrates the French way of life,\" UNESCO chief Audrey Asoulay said, adding: \"The baguette is a daily ritual, a structuring element of the meal, {{13}} to sharing and joy.\"","The exact origin of the baguette is not known. Some suggest the bread was ordered by Napoleon because it would be easier for soldiers to carry, {{14}} others suggest it came along later – an easy bread for workers to tear and share without the need of a knife in Paris. Others still credit an Austrian baker in the 1830s for its shape.","{{15}}, the baguette as we know it today was only officially named just over 100 years ago, in 1920. It was then that strict rules about what classed as a baguette were put in place – standardised at 80cm and 250g. It even had a fixed price until 1986.","By the middle of the 20th century, the baguette had won over the country. {{16}} the fact that since 1970 400 artisanal bakeries have closed down each year, the baguette remains key to French identity. Parisian baker Priscilla Hayertz acknowledged to AFP that it was \"a basic product\" but one \"that affects all socio-cultural categories, {{17}} you're rich or poor... it doesn't matter, everyone eats baguettes.\""],"items":[{"n":0,"options":[{"key":"A","text":"that"},{"key":"B","text":"so"},{"key":"C","text":"more"},{"key":"D","text":"most"}],"example":true,"answer":"C"},{"n":10,"options":[{"key":"A","text":"Therefore"},{"key":"B","text":"And yet"},{"key":"C","text":"Moreover"},{"key":"D","text":"Altogether"}]},{"n":11,"options":[{"key":"A","text":"it is due"},{"key":"B","text":"there’s something"},{"key":"C","text":"they are"},{"key":"D","text":"it was reason"}]},{"n":12,"options":[{"key":"A","text":"has been added"},{"key":"B","text":"is added"},{"key":"C","text":"must add"},{"key":"D","text":"had added"}]},{"n":13,"options":[{"key":"A","text":"contributing"},{"key":"B","text":"identified"},{"key":"C","text":"regarding"},{"key":"D","text":"considered"}]},{"n":14,"options":[{"key":"A","text":"all"},{"key":"B","text":"however"},{"key":"C","text":"while"},{"key":"D","text":"furthermore"}]},{"n":15,"options":[{"key":"A","text":"Otherwise"},{"key":"B","text":"Accidentally"},{"key":"C","text":"Meanwhile"},{"key":"D","text":"However"}]},{"n":16,"options":[{"key":"A","text":"In spite"},{"key":"B","text":"Considering"},{"key":"C","text":"Despite"},{"key":"D","text":"Along with"}]},{"n":17,"options":[{"key":"A","text":"whether"},{"key":"B","text":"either"},{"key":"C","text":"why"},{"key":"D","text":"both"}]}]}$mtr$::jsonb, null)
insert into public.task_keys (task_id, task) values ($mtr$2023-maj-emelt-L2$mtr$, $mtr${"id":"2023-maj-emelt-L2","number":2,"kind":"choice","layout":"inline","examType":"feleletválasztós szövegkiegészítés (A-D)","points":8,"instructions":["You are going to read an article about the success of the French baguette. Some words are missing from the text.","Choose the most appropriate answer from the options (A-D) for each gap (10-17) in the text."],"title":"FRENCH BAGUETTE GETS UNESCO HERITAGE STATUS","body":["There are few things {{0}} uniquely French than the humble baguette. {{10}}, the baguette has been in decline in recent years, as traditional bakeries struggle against the rise of large supermarkets and the increasing popularity of sourdough.","But now {{11}} to celebrate, as UNESCO adds the baguette to its cultural heritage list. The body announced that it {{12}} \"the special know-how and culture of baguette bread\" to its list of 600 other items, joining things like traditional tea making in China and a Korean mask dance – both also included for the first time in 2022.","Its inclusion \"celebrates the French way of life,\" UNESCO chief Audrey Asoulay said, adding: \"The baguette is a daily ritual, a structuring element of the meal, {{13}} to sharing and joy.\"","The exact origin of the baguette is not known. Some suggest the bread was ordered by Napoleon because it would be easier for soldiers to carry, {{14}} others suggest it came along later – an easy bread for workers to tear and share without the need of a knife in Paris. Others still credit an Austrian baker in the 1830s for its shape.","{{15}}, the baguette as we know it today was only officially named just over 100 years ago, in 1920. It was then that strict rules about what classed as a baguette were put in place – standardised at 80cm and 250g. It even had a fixed price until 1986.","By the middle of the 20th century, the baguette had won over the country. {{16}} the fact that since 1970 400 artisanal bakeries have closed down each year, the baguette remains key to French identity. Parisian baker Priscilla Hayertz acknowledged to AFP that it was \"a basic product\" but one \"that affects all socio-cultural categories, {{17}} you're rich or poor... it doesn't matter, everyone eats baguettes.\""],"items":[{"n":0,"options":[{"key":"A","text":"that"},{"key":"B","text":"so"},{"key":"C","text":"more"},{"key":"D","text":"most"}],"example":true,"answer":"C"},{"n":10,"options":[{"key":"A","text":"Therefore"},{"key":"B","text":"And yet"},{"key":"C","text":"Moreover"},{"key":"D","text":"Altogether"}],"answer":"B"},{"n":11,"options":[{"key":"A","text":"it is due"},{"key":"B","text":"there’s something"},{"key":"C","text":"they are"},{"key":"D","text":"it was reason"}],"answer":"B"},{"n":12,"options":[{"key":"A","text":"has been added"},{"key":"B","text":"is added"},{"key":"C","text":"must add"},{"key":"D","text":"had added"}],"answer":"D"},{"n":13,"options":[{"key":"A","text":"contributing"},{"key":"B","text":"identified"},{"key":"C","text":"regarding"},{"key":"D","text":"considered"}],"answer":"A"},{"n":14,"options":[{"key":"A","text":"all"},{"key":"B","text":"however"},{"key":"C","text":"while"},{"key":"D","text":"furthermore"}],"answer":"C"},{"n":15,"options":[{"key":"A","text":"Otherwise"},{"key":"B","text":"Accidentally"},{"key":"C","text":"Meanwhile"},{"key":"D","text":"However"}],"answer":"D"},{"n":16,"options":[{"key":"A","text":"In spite"},{"key":"B","text":"Considering"},{"key":"C","text":"Despite"},{"key":"D","text":"Along with"}],"answer":"C"},{"n":17,"options":[{"key":"A","text":"whether"},{"key":"B","text":"either"},{"key":"C","text":"why"},{"key":"D","text":"both"}],"answer":"A"}]}$mtr$::jsonb) on conflict (task_id) do update set task = excluded.task;
insert into public.tasks (id, exam_id, section, number, kind, exam_type, points, position, content, audio) values ($mtr$2023-maj-emelt-L3$mtr$, $mtr$2023-maj-emelt$mtr$, $mtr$language$mtr$, 3, $mtr$text$mtr$, $mtr$nyílt cloze (egy szó)$mtr$, 9, 7, $mtr${"id":"2023-maj-emelt-L3","number":3,"kind":"text","layout":"inline","examType":"nyílt cloze (egy szó)","points":9,"instructions":["You are going to read an article about an American musician. Some words are missing from the text.","Your task is to write the missing words on the dotted lines (18-26) after the text.","Use only one word in each gap."],"title":"THE ROCKIN’ GRANNY","body":["Somewhere in between Willie Nelson and Jimi Hendrix {{0}} Cordell Jackson, an American musician thought to be the first woman {{18}} produce, engineer and promote music on her own rock and roll music label. She was making music very {{19}} to the star band Velvet Underground before the world was even introduced {{20}} rock & roll. The Mississippi-born, ballgown-wearing guitarist played with more energy {{21}} any Indie band today, and during live performances, Cordell would strum on her guitar {{22}} fast that she would often break her guitar picks. At the height of her career, she appeared on MTV news and became known as “rock-and-roll granny”.","Jackson started playing the guitar at the age of 12. She began writing her own songs in her 20s after moving to Memphis, the later capital of rock & roll. “They did {{23}} have a name for “rock & roll” then, Cordell {{24}} MTV news in 1989. “I just always played it fast”.","In the 1960s and ’70s, she worked with local artists and soon became something {{25}} an icon on the Memphis music scene. She drove a yellow car and lived in a yellow house. Her first music video, {{26}} helped her gain nationwide fame, was filmed at that very house.","Jackson’s Moon Records label was the oldest continuously operating label in Memphis at the time of her death in 2004."],"grading":{"spelling":"strict"},"items":[{"n":0,"example":true,"accept":["was"]},{"n":18},{"n":19},{"n":20},{"n":21},{"n":22},{"n":23},{"n":24},{"n":25},{"n":26}]}$mtr$::jsonb, null)
insert into public.task_keys (task_id, task) values ($mtr$2023-maj-emelt-L3$mtr$, $mtr${"id":"2023-maj-emelt-L3","number":3,"kind":"text","layout":"inline","examType":"nyílt cloze (egy szó)","points":9,"instructions":["You are going to read an article about an American musician. Some words are missing from the text.","Your task is to write the missing words on the dotted lines (18-26) after the text.","Use only one word in each gap."],"title":"THE ROCKIN’ GRANNY","body":["Somewhere in between Willie Nelson and Jimi Hendrix {{0}} Cordell Jackson, an American musician thought to be the first woman {{18}} produce, engineer and promote music on her own rock and roll music label. She was making music very {{19}} to the star band Velvet Underground before the world was even introduced {{20}} rock & roll. The Mississippi-born, ballgown-wearing guitarist played with more energy {{21}} any Indie band today, and during live performances, Cordell would strum on her guitar {{22}} fast that she would often break her guitar picks. At the height of her career, she appeared on MTV news and became known as “rock-and-roll granny”.","Jackson started playing the guitar at the age of 12. She began writing her own songs in her 20s after moving to Memphis, the later capital of rock & roll. “They did {{23}} have a name for “rock & roll” then, Cordell {{24}} MTV news in 1989. “I just always played it fast”.","In the 1960s and ’70s, she worked with local artists and soon became something {{25}} an icon on the Memphis music scene. She drove a yellow car and lived in a yellow house. Her first music video, {{26}} helped her gain nationwide fame, was filmed at that very house.","Jackson’s Moon Records label was the oldest continuously operating label in Memphis at the time of her death in 2004."],"grading":{"spelling":"strict","maxWords":1},"items":[{"n":0,"example":true,"accept":["was"]},{"n":18,"accept":["to"]},{"n":19,"accept":["similar","akin"]},{"n":20,"accept":["to"]},{"n":21,"accept":["than"]},{"n":22,"accept":["so"]},{"n":23,"accept":["not"]},{"n":24,"accept":["told","informed"]},{"n":25,"accept":["of","like"]},{"n":26,"accept":["which"]}]}$mtr$::jsonb) on conflict (task_id) do update set task = excluded.task;
insert into public.tasks (id, exam_id, section, number, kind, exam_type, points, position, content, audio) values ($mtr$2023-maj-emelt-L4$mtr$, $mtr$2023-maj-emelt$mtr$, $mtr$language$mtr$, 4, $mtr$lines$mtr$, $mtr$soronkénti hibakeresés (felesleges szó vagy helyes sor)$mtr$, 9, 8, $mtr${"id":"2023-maj-emelt-L4","number":4,"kind":"lines","layout":"lines","examType":"soronkénti hibakeresés (felesleges szó vagy helyes sor)","points":9,"instructions":["You are going to read a joke about a married couple. In most lines there is one word that should not be there. It is either grammatically incorrect or does not fit in with the sense of the text.","Read the text and then copy the extra word in the space provided after each line.","Some lines may be correct. Indicate the correct line(s) with a tick ().","The task begins with two examples (0)."],"title":"HAPPILY MARRIED","intro":"","items":[{"n":"0a","example":true,"text":"At last, Tim decided to tie the knot with his long-time girlfriend. One","answer":null},{"n":"0b","example":true,"text":"evening, after their honeymoon, he was organizing his all golfing","answer":"all"},{"n":27,"text":"equipment. His wife was standing nearby to watching him. After a long"},{"n":28,"text":"period of the silence she finally said: “Tim, I've been thinking, now that"},{"n":29,"text":"we are married maybe it’s time you quit golfing. You should spend too"},{"n":30,"text":"much time on the golf course. You could probably get a good price as"},{"n":31,"text":"for your clubs.” A horrified expression appeared on Tim’s face."},{"n":32,"text":"His wife alarmingly said, “Darling, what’s wrong?\""},{"n":33,"text":"“It’s funny. For a minute you were beginning to have sound like my ex-"},{"n":34,"text":"wife,” he says. “Ex-wife!” she screams, “It’s a news to me you were"},{"n":35,"text":"married before!” “I wasn't,” he had replied."}]}$mtr$::jsonb, null)
