Some of the massive quotation websites are filled with misinformation,\" he told the BBC. \"These sites make the problem worse because many people incorrectly assume that large, professional-looking websites must contain valid data. The mission of QI is to provide information that is current, thorough, and very carefully documented.\" Sullivan writes with a pseudonym under which he wrote the book Hemingway Didn't Say That: The Truth Behind Familiar Quotations. So why do people keep pinning quotes on Maya Angelou? Basically, because the lines she did write were so good. Her quotability makes her a magnet for misquotation. Got a wise and compassionate line with no recorded owner? Just say it was Maya Angelou, the logic runs. Unless it's too spiritual, in which case try Gandhi or Mother Theresa. Or too sarcastic, when the obvious candidates are Oscar Wilde, Mark Twain or Winston Churchill. All eminently quotable men and women ̶ and too dead to disclaim the words they never said.","Summary A 2015 stamp had Maya Angelou's picture on it and a sentence that the {{0}} thought was by her. She is very popular and many people read her books, yet she is often {{18}}. Strangely enough, this even happened at an award-giving ceremony in the US in {{19}}. The sentence \"A bird doesn't sing because it has an answer, it sings because it has a song\" actually first appeared in a(n) {{20}}, but the {{21}} didn't sound too upset about the whole thing.","Anyone wanting to trace a quote to its genuine source can consult {{22}}, a website that promises to give accurate data. The man behind it, {{23}}, is determined to correct misinformation spread by quotation websites. Apart from Maya Angelou, people like Mother Theresa or Winston Churchill, among others, are frequently misquoted, too; the {{24}} one often credited with quite biting remarks."],"grading":{"spelling":"lenient","caseSensitive":false},"items":[{"n":0,"example":true,"accept":["US post"]},{"n":18,"accept":["misquoted","miscited","wrongly quoted","wrongly cited","badly quoted","badly cited","mistakenly quoted","mistakenly cited","incorrectly quoted","incorrectly cited","inaccurately quoted","inaccurately cited","imprecisely quoted","imprecisely cited"]},{"n":19,"accept":["2013"]},{"n":20,"accept":["children's book","1967 book","book"]},{"n":21,"accept":["author","writer","real author","real writer","true author","true writer","genuine author","genuine writer","original author","original writer","book’s author","book’s writer","children’s author","children’s writer"]},{"n":22,"accept":["Quote Investigator","QI"]},{"n":23,"accept":["Gregory Sullivan","Mr Sullivan","Sullivan"]},{"n":24,"accept":["latter","second","last","third"]}]}$mtr$::jsonb) on conflict (task_id) do update set task = excluded.task;
insert into public.tasks (id, exam_id, section, number, kind, exam_type, points, position, content, audio) values ($mtr$2025-okt-emelt-R4$mtr$, $mtr$2025-okt-emelt$mtr$, $mtr$reading$mtr$, 4, $mtr$choice$mtr$, $mtr$feleletválasztás a szöveg alapján (A-D)$mtr$, 6, 4, $mtr${"id":"2025-okt-emelt-R4","number":4,"kind":"choice","layout":"stems","examType":"feleletválasztás a szöveg alapján (A-D)","points":6,"instructions":["Read this article about how mechanical typewriters are coming back into fashion and then read the sentences that follow the text.","For each number (25-30) choose the option (A-D) that best corresponds to the text."],"title":"TYPEWRITER'S PROMISE OF A SIMPLER LIFE","body":["Like-the clip-clop of horses' hooves on city streets or the crackle when a vinyl LP reaches the end, it is a sound that almost but never quite vanished. Now the clatter of typewriter keys has become the latest echo from the pre-digital world to be heard again.","The price of vintage manual typewriters has increased dramatically as authors, poets, lovers and even fed-up parents discover the delights of \"slow writing\". For most it is less about nostalgia and more about the need to escape the \"noise\" of email, social media and the internet.","The typewriter revolution began in the United States but has spread to Britain, where dozens of old machines are being restored every week.","Repairmen are being persuaded to come out of retirement to help to feed demand from a generation that never heard the ping of a typewriter bell. Tom Knowles, 59, did his apprenticeship in typewriter repair over 40 years ago. He has never been so busy supplying spare parts and repairing vintage Olivettis.","\"People imagine my customers must be over 70 and can't get on with computers, but the reality is that most of them are under 30. A generation has suddenly discovered manual typewriters and thinks they are very cool,\" he said.","The typewriter's best known enthusiast is the actor Tom Hanks, who has a collection of more than a hundred. He has just finished a collection of short stories called Uncommon Type, each one featuring a different typewriter.","Mr Knowles said that people had gone back to manual typewriters because they found computers and smartphones, with their multiple functions, too distracting. \"A manual typewriter is a single purpose machine, it does nothing else. Because it doesn't have a delete or a correction key it concentrates your mind more on what you're writing.\"","Philip Chapman, from Wiltshire, sells about 500 machines a year through his website at up to £350 each. Mr Chapman said: \"We sell a lot to creative writers.\"","They also sell to parents who want to get their child away from their smartphone or tablet. \"There are boys, particularly, who are not interested in creative writing until you put a mechanical typewriter in front of them,\" Mr Chapman said. \"Suddenly they go 'wow' and the next moment they are writing.\""],"items":[{"n":0,"example":true,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Horses' hooves and vinyl LPs produce rather similar sounds."},{"key":"B","text":"LPs are a thing of the past; people just don't listen to them."},{"key":"C","text":"Typewriters have made a comeback on both sides of the Atlantic."},{"key":"D","text":"Some people love listening to the clatter of typewriter keys."}],"answer":"C"},{"n":25,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"\"Slow writing\" fans handwrite or use manual typewriters."},{"key":"B","text":"Manual typewriters cost more than they used to."},{"key":"C","text":"Parents are fed up with the noise computers make."},{"key":"D","text":"Most people feel nostalgic about the pre-digital world."}]},{"n":26,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"The US was first to rediscover manual typewriters."},{"key":"B","text":"Manual typewriters were redesigned in the US."},{"key":"C","text":"Tom Knowles' apprenticeship took a long time."},{"key":"D","text":"It is difficult to get spare parts for typewriters."}]},{"n":27,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"It is mostly old-age pensioners who buy mechanical typewriters."},{"key":"B","text":"Older and younger people are equally enthusiastic about mechanical typewriters."},{"key":"C","text":"It is the younger generations who find mechanical typewriters attractive."},{"key":"D","text":"Computer literate people are not interested in mechanical typewriters."}]},{"n":28,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"The actor Tom Hanks was the first to show an interest in typewriters."},{"key":"B","text":"Tom Hanks always uses a different typewriter when he writes."},{"key":"C","text":"Tom Hanks' new book contains a hundred short stories."},{"key":"D","text":"A typewriter plays a part in each of Tom Hanks' stories."}]},{"n":29,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"People get easily distracted when using a manual typewriter."},{"key":"B","text":"A typewriter makes it easier to concentrate on your thoughts."},{"key":"C","text":"The biggest problem with typewriters is that mistakes are not easy to correct."},{"key":"D","text":"Mr Knowles believes typewriters will never go out of fashion."}]},{"n":30,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Typewriters can have a surprising effect on boys."},{"key":"B","text":"Some boys cannot be motivated to learn to type."},{"key":"C","text":"Parents have started using manual typewriters."},{"key":"D","text":"Mr Chapman advises people to buy typewriters."}]}]}$mtr$::jsonb, null)
